hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27055","(27055) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Al-Safar, who said: I heard Abu Bakr bin Abi Musa It is narrated on the authority of Al-Baraa’ that when the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, woke up, he would say: Praise be to God who revived us after He caused us to die, and to Him is the resurrection. His people said: This, or something like this. And when he slept, he said: O God, in Your Name I live, and in Your Name. I am dying (Muslim 2083 and Ahmad 302)"
"27056","(27056) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Omar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wants to lie on his bed, let him remove inside his garment, then to dust his bed with it, for he does not know what he left behind it, then to lie on his part. The right hand, then to say, In Your Name, my Lord, I have placed myself at my side, and in You I lift it up. If I hold my soul, have mercy on it. You sent it, so protect it with the same way you protect your righteous servants. (Bukhari 7393. Tirmidhi 3401)"
"27057","(27057) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Saad ibn Ubaidah, on the authority of Al-Bara’ ibn Azib, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: When you take your bed, say: Oh God, I surrender myself to you and direct it. I turned to you, and I entrusted my affairs to you, and I turned my back to you out of desire and fear of you, with no refuge, no There is no refuge from you except in you. I believe in your book which you revealed, and in your prophet whom you sent. If you die, then die according to nature.\n(Bukhari 2471 Muslim 2081)"
"27058","(27058) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Abdullah bin Baba, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever says when he goes to bed, “There is no god but Allah alone, there is no partner with Him, to Him belongs the dominion, and to Him is praise, and He is above all.” A powerful thing. Glory be to God and with His praise, praise be to God. There is no god but God. God is greatest. His sins are forgiven, even if they are like foam. The sea\n(Ibn Hibban 5528)"
"27059","(27059) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Farwa bin Nawfal, on the authority of His father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to him: What brought you back? He said: You have come, O Messenger of God, to teach me something while I sleep. He said: When you go to bed, recite {Say, O you disbelievers} Then sleep at the end of it, for it is free from polytheism.\n(Abu Dawud 5016, Darmi 3427)"
"27060","(27060) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Nawfal Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of His father said: I said: O Messenger of God, tell me something that I should say in the morning and in the evening? He said: Recite {Say, O you disbelievers} and then sleep at the end of it, for it is a disavowal of polytheism."
"27061","(27061) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: If When you go to bed, say: In the name of God, in the path of God, and according to the religion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and when you enter the corpse His grave"
"27062","(27062) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Sawai, on the authority of Hafsiya, that the Prophet When he went to bed, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he would say: My Lord, protect me from Your torment on the day You resurrect Your servants.\n(Abu Dawud 5006. Ahmed 288)"
"27063","(27063) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man: O so-and-so, when you go to your bed, say: Oh God, I have surrendered myself to you, and I have directed my face to you, and I have turned to you. My back is to you. There is no refuge or refuge from you except in you. I believe in your book which you sent down, and in your prophet whom you sent. If you died that night, you died according to your nature, so if you wake up in the morning, you will do well. (Bukhari 7488 and Ahmed 299)"
"27064","(27064) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ifriqi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to a man from the Ansar: What do you say when you want to sleep? He said: I say in Your name, You have placed me beside me, so forgive me. He said: You have been forgiven. (Nasa’i 10606. Ahmad 173)"
"27065","(27065) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Our companions used to give us orders while we Boys, when we go to bed, we say “Tasbih” thirty-three times, “thank God” thirty-three times, and “Allahu Akbar” thirty-four times."
"27066","(27066) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: The Messenger of God When he went to bed, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he placed his right hand under his right cheek."
"27067","(27067) Ubaid bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Al-Mu’amil, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, When the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed the two rak’ahs of Fajr, he would lie down and place his right hand under his cheek. The right one\n(Bukhari 6261, Muslim 121)"
"27068","(27068) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he sleeps, he places his right hand under his cheek and says: Save me from your punishment on the day you resurrect your servants. (Ahmed 290)"
"27069","(27069) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, saying: Israel informed us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of His father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that when he slept, he would say: Oh God, protect me from your punishment on the day you gather your servants, He used to place his right hand under his cheek. (Tirmidhi 255. Ahmad 394)"
"27070","(27070) Abdullah bin Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Sa’id al-Maqbari, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you wants to lie on his bed, let him lie on The right side"
"27071","(27071) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salma bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abdul Rahman Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say in the morning: We have become a newcomer to the nature of Islam. And the word of sincerity, and the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, may God bless him and grant him peace, and the religion of our father Abraham, upright and Muslim, and he was not of The polytheists (Ahmad 407. Darami 2688)"
"27072","(27072) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Abu Aqeel narrated to me, on the authority of a previous person, on the authority of Abu Salam, the servant of the Messenger of God. God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There is no Muslim, human being, or servant who says three times in the evening and the morning: I am satisfied with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with Muhammad as prophet, but it is a duty upon God that He should be pleased with him on the Day of Resurrection.\n(Ibn Majah 3870)"
"27073","(27073) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Rab’i ibn Harash, on the authority of a man from Al-Nakh’, on the authority of Salman, who said: Who said if In the morning: Oh God, You are my Lord, You have no partner. We have entered the morning and the kingdom belongs to God. Praise be to God, He has no partner. And when An evening like that was an expiation for what had happened between them."
"27074","(27074) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Tamim ibn Salamah, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Sabra, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that He used to say in the morning and evening: Oh God, make me one of the best of Your servants in the morning or in the evening, a share of goodness. You distribute, or a light you guide, or mercy you spread, or sustenance you extend, or harm you uncover, or affliction you repel, or temptation You do it, or you repel evil."
"27075","(27075) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, who said: I said to Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab: What do you say then? What do you pray for in the morning and evening? He said: You say: I seek refuge in the Face of God the Most Generous, and in the Name of God the Great, and in the perfect Word of God, from the evil of the simple and common people, and from the evil of What You have created, O my Lord, and the evil of what You are taking by His command, and the evil of this day, and the evil of what comes after it, and the evil of this world. And the Hereafter"
"27076","(27076) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Musa al-Jinni, who said: A man narrated to me, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, that he said: Who He said (Glory be to God when the evening comes and when you become in the morning) until he finished the verses three times, when he realized what he had missed from his day. And whoever says it at night will realize what he missed during the day. (Abu Dawud 5037)"
"27077","(27077) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Salih, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Ayyash, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Whoever says in the morning, “There is no god but God alone, without any partner, to Him belongs the kingdom and to Him.” Praise, and He is Able to do all things. He had as many slaves from the descendants of Ishmael, and ten good deeds were recorded for him, and He granted He was burdened with ten bad deeds, and he was raised ten degrees because of them, and he was under protection from Satan until the evening, and when He spent the evening like this until the morning. (Ibn Majah 3867. Ahmed 60)"
"27078","(27078) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Salih, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, that Omar wrote: Do not mix with reeds."
"27079","(27079) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Bakr Al-Ghasaniy, on the authority of Damra bin Habib, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, regarding the siwak and the basil and pomegranate leaves, and he said: “It relieves the sweat of leprosy.”"
"27080","(27080) Yahya ibn Adam narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Bara’, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by May God bless him and grant him peace upon a gathering of the Ansar, and he said: If you refuse not to sit, then guide me to the way, return the greeting, and help. The oppressed (Tirmidhi 2726. Ahmad 282)"
"27081","(27081) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Musa bin Ubaidah narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Khalid, on the authority of Malik bin Al-Tayhan, who said: A group of us gathered at the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we said: O Messenger of God, we are the people of the bastard and the people of Your Excellency, we sit in these gatherings, so what do you command us to do? He said: Give the gatherings their due. We said: What is their due? He said: Lower your gaze, return the greeting, guide the blind, and enjoin what is right. And refrain from evil. (Musnad 685)"
"27082","(27082) Affan told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Othman bin Hakim told us, he said: Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha said: My father told me, he said: Abu Talha said: We were sitting in the courtyard, and the Messenger of God passed by us. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: What is the matter with you when you avoid gatherings in the hills? He said: We said: O Messenger of God, we sat without any harm, studying and talking. He said: So give the gatherings their due rights. He said: We said: What is her right, O Messenger of God? He said: Lowering your gaze, returning your greetings, and speaking well. (Ahmad 30, Abu Ali 1417)"
"27083","(27083) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughul, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Al-Rabi’ bin Khuthaym has not sat in a council since He girded himself with a garment and said: I fear that a man will be wronged and I will not support him, or that a man will slander another man so I will appoint a witness against him, and I will not I will lower my gaze and not guide the way, or the pregnant woman will fall and I will not bear the burden for her."
"27084","(27084) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of the common people, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, who said: They were disliked when they took seats. To expose it to the foolish."
"27085","(27085) Mahboub Al-Qawariri narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sa’b ibn Hakim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: I came to Umar ibn Al-Khattab, so he started saying: O my nephew. Then he asked me, and I was related to him, so he knew that my father did not introduce you to Islam, so he started saying: : Oh my son, oh my son."
"27086","(27086) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi, he said: He did not ask One of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of the Antichrist, more than I asked him, so he said: Yes, he is a son, and what will befall you from him?\n(Muslim 1693. Ibn Majah 4073)"
"27087","(27087) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Abi and Jazā’ al-Sa’di, on the authority of a man from Muzaynā, on the authority of Omar bin Abi Salamah The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was brought food and said: O Omar, my son, name God and eat with your right hand and eat from Here you go\n(Abu Dawud 3771, Ahmed 26)"
"27088","(27088) Affan narrated to us, saying: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ja’d Abu Uthman, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to him: O my son. (Muslim 1693; Abu Dawud 4925)"
"27089","(27089) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Amara ibn Zazan, on the authority of Makhul al-Azdi, who said: Ibn Umar was asked about a man who is deprived of Samarkand, or from Khorasan, or from Kufa, and he said: I wish we could spare our time, my sons."
"27090","(27090) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Jamriya, who said: Iyas narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Qais bin Abbad, that Ubayy bin Ka’b said to him: O my son, may God not harm you."
"27091","(27091) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, that he said: O my sons."
"27092","(27092) Ishaq bin Sulaiman al-Razi told us, on the authority of Nu’aym, who said: I asked Asim about God’s saying: {So he called her from beneath her} He said: {beneath it} open, I said: from whom are you narrating? He said: About a button, my son."
"27093","(27093) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: Abu Wael said to me, “O my sons.”"
"27094","(27094) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaidullah, who said: I said to the son of a friend of mine: O son, think about it. That is Abraham."
"27095","(27095) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Shutair bin Shikal, that a woman She said to him: Son. He said: You gave birth to me. She said: No. He said: Did you breastfeed me? She said: No. He said: Why are you lying?"
"27096","(27096) Zaid bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Hussein narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman. On the authority of his mother, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who says good, does good, or does good is not lying. Between two (Bukhari 2692, Muslim 2011)"
"27097","(27097) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Asma bint Yazeed said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Lying is not permissible except in three cases: a man’s lie His wife to please her, or to reconcile people, or to lie in war. (Tirmidhi 1939. Ahmad 461)"
"27098","(27098) Zayd bin Harun told us: Hisham bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever covers his Muslim brother in this world, God will see him in This world and the hereafter, and whoever relieves his brother of the distress of this world, God will relieve him of the distress of this day. Resurrection, and God will help the servant as long as the servant is helping his brother. (Abdul Razzaq 18933 and Ahmed 514)"
"27099","(27099) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Whoever relieves a Muslim of the distress of this world, God will relieve him of the distress of the Hereafter on the Day of Resurrection. Resurrection, and whoever protects a Muslim, Allah will see him in this world and the hereafter, and whoever makes things easy for someone in difficulty, Allah will make things easy for him in this world. And the Hereafter, and God helps the servant as long as the servant helps his brother. (Abu Dawud 4854, Hakim 377)"
"27100","(27100) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, who said: Ibn Masoud came and was told: This is so-and-so. His beard dripped with wine, so Abdullah said: We have been forbidden from spying, but if anything from him appears to us, we will take it. With it"
"27101","(27101) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabi, on the authority of Abu Idris, who said: May God not tear the veil of a servant. In his heart is an atom's weight of goodness."
"27102","(27102) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, saying: I heard Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talhahi, saying: Shayb narrated to me. Al-Khudhari, that he witnessed Urwah narrating Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: God does not cover a servant in this world except that God will cover him in the Hereafter. (Muslim 2002, Ahmed 145)"
"27103","(27103) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Abd al-Wahid bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: Whoever extinguishes the evil of a believer, it is as if he had revived a dead person."
"27104","(27104) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salma narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Asir Bin Jabir, that when Uwais al-Qarni narrated, his narration would enter our hearts in a place where no other narration would reach."
"27105","(27105) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salama narrated to us, on the authority of Yasar bin Salama, on the authority of Shar bin Hawshab, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If a man speaks to a people, then his speech takes place in their hearts just as it takes place in his heart."
"27106","(27106) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Abu Ghaffar, on the authority of Abu Tamimah Al-Hajmi, on the authority of Abu Jari Al-Hujaimi said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: I said: Are you the Messenger of God? He said: Yes, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, return to me. He said: Do not curse anyone. He said: I have not cursed anyone, whether a slave, nor a free man, nor A sheep or a camel."
"27107","(27107) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Hamid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The greatest sin in the sight of God is for a man to curse his mother. They said: How is it? Does a man curse his mother-in-law? He said: If someone curses a man’s father, he will curse his father, and if he curses his mother, he will curse his mother.\n(Bukhari 5973, Abu Dawud 5098)"
"27108","(27108) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of his father, who said: He conveys the message to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: One of the people who raise usury is a man being kind to his brother by cursing him, and the greatest of sins is cursing a man. And his parents. It was said: O Messenger of God, how can he insult his parents? He said: He curses people, so people curse him with what. (Tabarani 899)"
"27109","(27109) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Asim, who said: I never saw Abu Wa’il insult anything except that he mentioned Al-Hajjaj. He passed by and said: Oh God, feed him with food from a breastfed animal that will not make him fat or relieve him of hunger. Then he said: If he is more beloved to you."
"27110","(27110) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Fudail, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: No. He who has in his heart the weight of a mustard seed of pride will enter Paradise."
"27111","(27111) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Al-Aghar Abi Muslim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: God says: Greatness is my garment, and pride is my robe, so whoever competes with me for one of them I threw him into the fire."
"27112","(27112) Affan narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, on the authority of Abd God said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: No one who has in his heart a mustard seed’s worth of arrogance will enter Paradise. And no one who has as much faith as a mustard seed in his heart will enter Hell. (Muslim 93 Abu Dawud 4088)"
"27113","(27113) Ali bin Musir told us, on the authority of Abu Hayyan, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah bin Amr and Ibn Umar met So they went away to each other, then each one of them went to his companions, and Ibn Umar went away crying, and they said to him: What is the matter? Does he make you cry? He said: The one who claimed this made me cry because he heard it from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No one enters Paradise in His heart is as heavy as a mustard seed, full of arrogance. (Ahmed 164)"
"27114","(27114) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Amr bin Shu’aib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: He said The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The arrogant will appear on the Day of Resurrection as atoms like the images of men, their height being all One of the little ones. He said: Then they will be taken to a prison in Hell, called Paul, with fire surmounting above them. They will be made to drink of The clay of immorality, the juice of the people of Hell. (Tirmidhi 2492. Ahmad 179)"
"27115","(27115) Ibn Idris, Ibn Uyaynah, and Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Muammar ibn Abi Hayya, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Adiy ibn al-Khayyar, who said: Umar said: When a servant is proud, he promises He descended, and God cast him down to the earth, and said: “Hustle! God has humbled you,” for in Himself He is great, but in people’s souls He is small. It is even more despicable to people than a pig."
"27116","(27116) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali ibn Ata, who said: I heard Nafi’ ibn Asim, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr. He said: No arrogant person will enter Jerusalem."
"27117","(27117) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam ibn Al-Harith, on the authority of Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: No dead person enters Paradise. (Bukhari 6056 and Muslim 169)"
"27118","(27118) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhaifi, who said: We were talking about: No. He enters Paradise for a number of times. (Muslim 1011, Ahmad 168)"
"27119","(27119) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maymun, who said: When God raised up Moses as a saved person, he saw a man Clinging to the throne, he said: O Lord, who is this? He said: He is a righteous servant of My servants. If you wish, I can tell you his deeds. He said: O Lord, tell me. He said: He did not walk. With gossip"
"27120","(27120) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: It was ours. A foreigner neighbour. She fell ill and began to say upon death: This is so-and-so who wallowed in mud. When she died, we asked about The man, he said: He said: There was nothing wrong with him except that he used to walk with gossip."
"27121","(27121) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Mujahid and Salem bin Abi al-Ja’d, On the authority of Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Mannan does not enter the jinn."
"27122","(27122) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, who said: I heard Nafi’ bin Asim narrating on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: No man will enter the enclosure of Jerusalem."
"27123","(27123) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ali ibn Mudarrak, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Kharsha ibn al-Hurr, on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: There are three to whom God will not speak on the Day of Resurrection, nor will He look at them. Nor will He purify them, and they will have a painful punishment. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, recited it three times, and Abu Dharr said: They were disappointed and lost. Who are they, O Messenger of God? He said: The one who gives way, the one who gives money, and the one who spends his goods are spoiled by false oaths.\n(Muslim 171, Abu Dawud 4085, Ahmad 148)"
"27124","(27124) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Al-Ja’d, on the authority of Nubait bin Shurayt, on the authority of Jaban On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: No human being will enter Paradise."
"27125","(27125) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, who said: When God raised up Moses as a saved person, he saw A man clinging to the throne said: O Lord, who is this? He said: He is a righteous servant of My servants. If you wish, I can tell you his deeds. He said: O Lord, tell me. He said: He was not envious of people’s actions. God gave them of His bounty."
"27126","(27126) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Anas, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: Indeed, envy consumes good deeds just as fire consumes wood. (Ibn Majah 4210; Abu Ali 3444)"
"27127","(27127) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Yazid Al-Raqqashi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Envy almost overcomes predestination, and poverty almost becomes disbelief."
"27128","(27128) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Raja’i, on the authority of Al-Hasan, “And they will not find in their breasts any portion of what they were given.” He said: envy."
"27129","(27129) Abd al-Salam narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, in the Almighty’s saying: {And those who, when they spend, are not extravagant nor They procured, and in the midst of that there was a solid state. There it is."
"27130","(27130) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Amr ibn Qais, on the authority of al-Manhal, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr: {And what Whatever you spend, he will replace it, and He is the Best of Providers.} He said: Without extravagance, nor frugality."
"27131","(27131) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Yahya bin Al-Jazzar, on the authority of Abu Al-Ubaidin, He asked Ibn Masoud about extravagance, and he said: spending money on something other than its proper purpose."
"27132","(27132) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Dawud, who said: I said to Al-Hasan: Buy something for your wife during the year. Is this extravagant for twenty dirhams? He said: This is not an extravagance."
"27133","(27133) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Misra, on the authority of Tawoos, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Wear whatever you want. And eat whatever you want, as long as two traits have failed you: extravagance, or imagination."
"27134","(27134) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Suqi, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: A man asked him about his waste. Money. He said: If God provides you with sustenance, and you spend it in what He has forbidden to you."
"27135","(27135) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of the common people, he said: Ka’b said: Spend for a successor that will come to you."
"27136","(27136) Affan narrated to us, on the authority of Sakin bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Al-Hijri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: He who is frugal is not high. (Ahmad 447. Tabarani 10118)"
"27137","(27137) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf, on the authority of Abu al-Siriya ibn al-Hasan, who said: There is no extravagance in food."
"27138","(27138) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Ziyad, the client of Musab, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that the companions of the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. They asked him: What did we spend on our families? He said: Whatever you spend on your families without extravagance or frugality, it is for the sake of God. (Bayhaqi 6554)"
"27139","(27139) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu Kathir, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Beware of stinginess, for it destroyed you before you. He commanded them to be stingy, so they disobeyed, to be miserly, so they were stingy, and to be immoral, so they committed immorality. (Abu Dawud 1695; Ahmed 191)"
"27140","(27140) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Safwan ibn Sulaym, on the authority of Husain ibn Al-Lajlaj, On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Stinginess and faith do not coexist in the heart of a Muslim man."
"27141","(27141) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Marwan, on the authority of Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The worst thing in a man is shameful stinginess and immoral cowardice.\n(Abu Dawud 2503, Ahmed 302)"
"27142","(27142) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Mundakir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If the money of the two Bahrains had come, I would have given you such-and-such. So I went to Abu Bakr and said: Be stingy with me. He said: What a helper? Is it worse than miserliness? You have not asked for anything except that I want to give it to you. (Bukhari 2598, Muslim 1806)"
"27143","(27143) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Jami’ ibn Shaddad, on the authority of Al-Aswad ibn Hilal, who said: A man came to Abd God said: I feared that these verses would befall me: {And whoever is saved from his own miserliness} the verses, I cannot give him anything. I can bear to prevent him. Abdullah said: That is stinginess, and what a miserable thing is stinginess."
"27144","(27144) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of Ibn Al-Ahmas, who said: I said to Abu Dhar: A hadith that reached me. Are you talking to him on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: I heard it from him and I said it, so he mentioned three that God disapproves of: the stingy, the ungrateful, and the conceited."
"27145","(27145) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, and Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, that The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: Oh God, I seek refuge in You from miserliness."
"27146","(27146) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Omar, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, used to seek refuge from miserliness."
"27147","(27147) Shababi told us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq told us, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun, on the authority of Omar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, likewise."
"27148","(27148) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to seek refuge from Stinginess"
"27149","(27149) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Suhaim, on the authority of Talha bin Ubaid Allah bin Kariz, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, God is generous, loves generosity, loves high morals, and hates immorality.\n(Abdul Razzaq 2015, Rule 628)"
"27150","(27150) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, who said: The Prophet used to pray May God bless him and grant him peace from Saad ibn Ubadah. His eyelids revolved with him wherever he went from his wives, and he used to say in his supplication: Oh God. Grant me wealth, for only wealth is good for an effective person."
"27151","(27151) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, that Saad bin Ubadah used to pray to God to give me praise. And bestow upon me glory, and there is no glory except by means of action, and there is no effect except by money. O God, let not a little be good for me, nor be good for me.\n(Ibn Saad 614, Hakim 253)"
"27152","(27152) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: I caught Saad bin Ubadah while he was calling Ali. Atmaha: Whoever loves fat and meat, let him go to Saad bin Ubadah, and after that I will find his son praying for him, and I was I was walking on the road to Medina when I was a young man, and Abdullah bin Omar passed by me, heading to his land in the forest, and he said: O boy, look. You saw someone calling on Utam Saad bin Ubadah, so I looked and said: No, and he said: You are right."
"27153","(27153) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Qais bin Sa’d bin Ubadah traveled towards He went to Medina and had companions with him, so he began to slaughter a mighty animal every day until he reached Sarar."
"27154","(27154) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was And when he greeted in the evening, he divided people from the people of Saffah among people from his companions, and the man would go with another man, and the other With two men, and the man with three, until he mentioned ten. He said: Saad bin Ubadah used to return to his family every night. With eighty of them for the evening."
"27155","(27155) Ali told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was more generous than the sent fragrance. (Bukhari 3220, Ahmed 230)"
"27156","(27156) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Saad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was the most generous of people with goodness, and he was the most generous when he met them. Gabriel\n(Bukhari 1902 and Muslim 1803)"
"27157","(27157) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Salama bin Abi Yahya Al-Ansari, who said: I saw Anas bin Malik sitting To Saria"
"27158","(27158) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Al-Mukhtar bin Saad, who said: I saw Al-Qasim bin Muhammad sitting at his pole."
"27159","(27159) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Thabit bin Qais, who said: I saw Nafi bin Jubayr sitting at his pole."
"27160","(27160) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I saw Ubaid Allah bin Abdullah sitting next to Sarah"
"27161","(27161) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, who said: Abraham would not sit on a cylinder."
"27162","(27162) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, who said: I did not see Salim bin Abdullah sitting at my pole."
"27163","(27163) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abu Qatada al-Ansari descended upon us. Then a star struck, and we followed it with our sight, but it prevented us from that. (Ahmed 2998 Hakim 286)"
"27164","(27164) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he did not see any harm in a man following his sight. The planet when it is thrown at it."
"27165","(27165) Qubaisa narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Abu His followers are like the hadith of Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Asim."
"27166","(27166) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, he said: Abu Aqeel told us, he said: Amr bin Khaled Al-Qurashi told us, he said: I heard Zaid Ibn Ali narrates, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Ali, that when he saw a star descending, he would say: Oh God Aim at it and strike it, and protect us from the evil that follows."
"27167","(27167) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jarir, on the authority of Mutarrif, who said : None of you should lie twice, saying to something: Nothing, it is nothing."
"27168","(27168) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Ibn Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: He used to say: This knowledge is religion, so look. From whom are you taking it? (Dharmi 419)"
"27169","(27169) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He hated to say: There is no one in the house. There is no harm in him saying: There is no one in the house."
"27170","(27170) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zayd narrated to us, saying: Ayyub said: Saeed bin Jubayr narrated to us one day. So I got up to him and said: Bring him back. He said: I milk and drink every hour."
"27171","(27171) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Jabbar, he said: I heard Ibn Shihab say: Repeating a hadith is more severe than Transporting stones"
"27172","(27172) Ali narrated to us, saying: Abu Hayyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abaya, who said: Ibn Umar performed the ablution, so I got up, on his right, he emptied He poured water on him, and when he finished, he looked at me and said: Where did you get this literature? So I said: From my grandfather, Rafi’. He said: He said: Congratulations to you."
"27173","(27173) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If you meet your brother, do not ask him who Where did you come from? And where are you going? And do not look at your brother."
"27174","(27174) Ismail Ibn Aliyya narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj Al-Sawaf, he said: Yahya Ibn Abi Kathir narrated to me, saying: He informed me, The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say: If one of you passes by an inclined target or a huge shell, let him walk quickly. And may he ask God for well-being."
"27175","(27175) Hatem bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Imran Al-Qasir, who said: Sa’id bin Sulayman informed me, on the authority of Yazid bin Naamah Al-Dhabi said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a man has a brother to another man, let him ask him about his name and the name of his father. And whoever is, he is more conducive to affection. (Abu Naim 181)"
"27176","(27176) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saw A man asked about him, and a man said: I know his face, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: It is not that I know him."
"27177","(27177) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, and more, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubaid bin Al-Hasan, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: A man’s spending on his family is charity."
"27178","(27178) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: Among the expenses that are multiplied by seven hundred times your expenses. A man is responsible for himself and his family."
"27179","(27179) Zayd bin Harun told us, saying: Sha’bā informed us, on the authority of Adiy bin Thabit, on the authority of Abdullah bin Zayd, On the authority of Abu Masoud, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: A man’s spending on his family is charity. (Bukhari 55. Muslim 695)"
"27180","(27180) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, saying: Bashar bin Abi Saif narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Iyad bin Ghataif, who said: We entered upon Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, and he said: I heard the Messenger of God. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he says: Whoever spends on his family, or removes harm from the path, his good deeds will be multiplied ten times as much."
"27181","(27181) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Hisham bin Urwah narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Marawahih, on the authority of Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, which deed is best? He said: Faith in God and jihad in His way. He said: I said: Which of the slaves is better? He said: Its value is with its family and the most expensive in price. I said: What if I cannot bear it? He said: You appoint a craftsman, or you make for a fool. He said: What if I cannot? He said: So keep people away from evil, for it is a charity that you give in charity to yourself."
"27182","(27182) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Barda, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: Every Muslim owes charity. He said: It was said: What do you think if he does not find it? He said: He works with his hands to benefit himself and gives in charity. He said: What do you think if he cannot? He said: He helps the wrapped pilgrim. He said: What do you think if he is not able? He said: He enjoins what is right or good. He said: What do you think if he does not do it? He said: Refrain from evil, for it is the truth.\n(Bukhari 1445. Muslim 699)"
"27183","(27183) Abu Asama narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of the Tamar dinar, on the authority of Aoun bin Abdullah, who said: Abdullah was He was walking with some of his companions one day, and the length of his sandal was cut off, so it was restored. Some of the people said to him: O Abu Abd. The Most Gracious, will you recover on a path? He said: It is not the case that there are not many fences, but they are a disaster."
"27184","(27184) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abdullah bin Khalifa, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, He was cut off and recovered, and he said: Whatever happened to you is a disaster."
"27185","(27185) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us: Shayban informed us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, who said : Omar’s sandal was cut off and he said: To Allah we belong and to Him we shall return. So they said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is the kiss of your sandal? He said: Yes, everything that befalls a believer is a calamity."
"27186","(27186) Hussein bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Jarir bin Hazim narrated to us, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Say: The Seal of the Prophets, And do not say: There is no prophet after him."
"27187","(27187) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, who said: Amir told us, he said: A man said to Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba: May God bless him and grant him peace. Ali is the Seal of the Prophets, there is no prophet after him. Al-Mughirah said: It is sufficient for you if you say: The Seal of the Prophets, for we used to narrate, That Jesus is going out, so if he is going out, then it was before and after him."
"27188","(27188) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade killing ants. And the bees\n(Abu Dawud 5225. Ahmed 332)"
"27189","(27189) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If ants harm you, kill them."
"27190","(27190) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Dinar, who said: I saw Abu Al-Aaliyah who saw ants on a carpet and killed them."
"27191","(27191) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Nafi`, on the authority of Sulayman al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: We disperse ants with water. That means if you hurt us."
"27192","(27192) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, who said: My father said to me: Did you write? He said: I said: Yes, he said: I objected? I said: No, he said: You did not write. (Ramaramzi 718)"
"27193","(27193) Ismail bin Ayyash narrated to us, on the authority of Siwar bin Abdullah, who said: Muhammad hated to raise the story of no He knows what is in it."
"27194","(27194) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I heard Abu Ishaq narrating, he said: Abdullah hated to The man jumped to his right while not praying, and Aban said to him: About whom? He said: On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Zaid, on the authority of Abdullah."
"27195","(27195) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Ibn Sirin had a door on his left that was blocked, and he used to turn around. To it, and He spits on it."
"27196","(27196) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Saad bin Ibrahim, he said: I heard him say: From the mind of a man The location of his slug."
"27197","(27197) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, who said: Abdullah was He was sitting facing the direction of the direction, so he wanted to spit to his left, but he was busy and decided to spit to his right."
"27198","(27198) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, that Mu’adh spit one day, on the right side of him. Then he said: Ha, I have not done this since I accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or he said: Since I converted to Islam."
"27199","(27199) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Abu Hilal narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abu Bakr spit or spit on When he was sick, he fell ill with her, and he said: I only did it once, or he said: Other than that, this time."
"27200","(27200) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I apologized to Abraham for something he had reported about me, and he said: No. Apologize, we have apologized to you without apologizing."
"27201","(27201) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Misra, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Abi Rafi’ al-Tai’i said: I came to Abu Bakr and said: You ordered me to do what you ordered me to do and I entered into what I entered into. He still apologized. Until you excuse me."
"27202","(27202) Hafs, Ibn Numayr, and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: ‘Abdullah said, “Fear me,” and Hafs said: Beware of excuses, for many of them are lies."
"27203","(27203) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, who said: Shurayh came out to us. He apologizes."
"27204","(27204) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, he said: I was walking with al-Hakam, and we saw Abu Ma`shar, and he said The ruling: This has reached him about something that you said, “No, by God, there is no god but Him.” He said: When Abu A group of people apologized to the arbitrator and said: I swore to my people that I did not say what you heard from me."
"27205","(27205) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his uncle, he said: I heard Al-Sha’bi say: Abraham came to me to apologize to me for something. He informed me about it."
"27206","(27206) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, that a man told me about Abu Issa: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: Indeed, Jesus has no father."
"27207","(27207) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar bin Hafs, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of his father that Omar hit a son of his who referred to me as my father, Jesus, and said: Jesus has no father. (Abdul Razzaq 19857)"
"27208","(27208) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Excessive laughter kills the heart. (Bukhari 252. Ibn Majah 4217)"
"27209","(27209) Affan told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The believer’s laughter is a heedlessness of his heart."
"27210","(27210) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Aoun, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would not laugh except with a smile. And he does not turn around except together."
"27211","(27211) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Omar has reached the age of the Prophet, that there is no one who works for him. So Omar wrote to him: Say, for I was told that Satan does not speak. Mujahid said: Indeed, the devils do not speak."
"27212","(27212) Muhammad bin Bishr and Wakee’ narrated to us, saying: Mis’ar narrated to us, saying: Thabit bin Ubaid narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abu Layla, on the authority of Khawat bin Jubayr, who was Badriya, said: Sleeping at the beginning of the day is rags, the middle of the day is good-natured, and the end of it is foolishness."
"27213","(27213) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid bin Jabir, on the authority of Makhoul, that it was He dislikes sleeping after the afternoon prayer, and he said: He fears for his companion that he will be obsessive about him."
"27214","(27214) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: The Messenger passed by God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a man lying on his stomach, and he said: This is a position that God does not like.\n(Tirmidhi 2768 and Ahmad 287)"
"27215","(27215) Al-Hasan bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Shayban narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, that Aisha bin Qais bin Takhfiya narrated it, on the authority of his father, who said: My father was one of the companions of the Safas. He said: While I am sleeping on My stomach was filled with magic when a man pushed me with his foot and said: This is the woman that God hates. I raised my head and behold... The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. (Abu Dawud 5001, Ahmed 429)"
"27216","(27216) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, saying: Asim bin Kulayb narrated to us, on the authority of his father. On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In all his sermons, there is no tashahhud like the tashahud. Leprosy (Tirmidhi 1106. Abu Dawud 4808)"
"27217","(27217) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Bakhtari, who said: Every pilgrim There is no tash-hud in it, so it is tash-hud."
"27218","(27218) Aswad bin Amir narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, saying: I heard Humayd bin Hilal say: All his speeches are not Therein you bear witness, therein you declare."
"27219","(27219) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Huraira, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Every meaningful speech does not begin with praise be to God, so it is I cut off\n(Abu Dawud 4807, Ahmed 359)"
"27220","(27220) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abu Al-Muhazam, on the authority of Abu Huraira, that He saw a man with a boy running behind him, so he said: Carry him, for he is your Muslim brother, and his soul is like yours."
"27221","(27221) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Yusuf bin Al-Muhajir, who said: I saw Abu Ja’far riding on a mule, or A mule with a boy walking beside it."
"27222","(27222) Abu Osama narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bai. He said: Shammisa narrated to me, she said: I heard Aisha, and she was asked about etiquette. The orphan, and she said: I will beat one of them until he feels happy."
"27223","(27223) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Arni, that a man said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: How should I beat an orphan? He said: Hit him as you used to hit your son. (Tabari 260)"
"27224","(27224) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far Al-Khutmiy, that his father asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab Or he said: Send a friend of his and I am with him to ask him: Why does a man beat his orphan? He said: Why does a man hit his son? Abu Ja`far said: He asked Muhammad bin Ka’b and he said something like that."
"27225","(27225) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I read a book that contained whatever God and the Emir wished. He said: Whatever the Emir wished. After God"
"27226","(27226) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Hudhayf, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not say: What God willed and so-and-so willed, but say: What God willed, then so-and-so willed.\n(Abu Dawud 4941, Ahmed 384)"
"27227","(27227) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Asam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: A man came to the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he told him some words, and he said: “Whatever God wills, and you will.” He said: “By God, you have made me just.” Nay, as He willed. God (Ibn Majah 2117 and Ahmed 214)"
"27228","(27228) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Zur’a ibn Muslim ibn Jarhad, on the authority of his grandfather, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He saw him in the mosque, wearing a cloak, and his thigh was exposed, and he said: The thigh is part of the private parts. (Tirmidhi 2798 and Abu Dawud 4010)"
"27229","(27229) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Ibn Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: Omar said: The man’s thigh is from the private parts."
"27230","(27230) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: The thigh is from the private parts."
"27231","(27231) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The thigh in the mosque emerging from the private parts."
"27232","(27232) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Yahya, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The thigh is part of the private parts. (Tirmidhi 2796 and Ahmad 275)"
"27233","(27233) Ja’far bin Aoun narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfy, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, my brother between Salman and Abu Darda’. (Bukhari 1968 and Tirmidhi 2413)"
"27234","(27234) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of Bashir ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Ka’b ibn Malik, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a brother between Al-Zubayr and Ka’b bin Malik. (Ibn Saad 102)"
"27235","(27235) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Abu Farwa, who said: Ibn Abi Layla said: The Messenger of God was May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, my brother between Zaid and Hamza."
"27236","(27236) Qubaysah narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was his brother. Between Abi Talha and Abi Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah. (Hakim 268)"
"27237","(27237) Affan narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace. My brother between Awf bin Malik and Al-Saab bin Jathama."
"27238","(27238) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hikam, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him He greeted Ali and said, “You are my brother and companion.” (Tirmidhi 3720 and Ahmad 230)"
"27239","(27239) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, saying: Humaid told us, on the authority of Anas, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was his brother among `Abd. Al-Rahman bin Awf and Saad bin Al-Rabi’. (Bukhari 2049. Ahmad 271)"
"27240","(27240) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A man does not refuse to take from the dirhams of a friend."
"27241","(27241) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: You have seen us, and the Muslim man is not more deserving. With a dinar or a dirham from his Muslim brother."
"27242","(27242) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, who said: Alqamiya said to him: O Abu Amr, He said: Labayk, and he said to him: Alqamiya: Labyk."
"27243","(27243) Affan narrated to us, saying: Abu Awani narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: When he was called, he would say: “Lybi.” God, and he does not say: Here you are."
"27244","(27244) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Saad bin Yusuf bin Yaqoub, who said: They said to Tawoos about a slave of his, and he said: He has no money to write to him, nor is he righteous so I can marry him. He used to hate being beaten, and he used to say: Chain."
"27245","(27245) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Taman, on the authority of the one who narrated to him, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, that it was He hates it for a man to put a flag around his servant’s neck."
"27246","(27246) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he hated for a man to be put on the neck of his servant. The righteousness"
"27247","(27247) Ibn Abi Zayd narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, that he said to a man And he mentioned his wife and said: Tie her down."
"27248","(27248) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Usama bin Zaid, on the authority of Muhammad bin al-Mundakir, on the authority of Jabir, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, says: Ask God for useful knowledge and seek refuge in God from knowledge that is of no benefit. (Bukhari 3220, Ahmed 230)"
"27249","(27249) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ghalib al-Abdi, on the authority of a man from Banu Nimir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, Or his father’s grandfather. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, my father is offering you peace. He said: Peace be upon you and your father. I said: O Messenger. By God, my people want to know me. He said: There must be a serf, and the serf will be in Hell."
"27250","(27250) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, on the authority of a man whom he did not name, who heard Anas say: Woe to the sophisticates. And the captains, woe to the trustworthy ones. On the Day of Resurrection, one of them would have liked to have been hung from the chandelier. (Ahmad 531, Abu Ali 6189)"
"27251","(27251) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaqiq, on the authority of Habib bin Hudaydah, who said: Because Being cut off is dearer to me than being a commoner for ten years."
"27252","(27252) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Hakim, who said: Abdullah ibn Uthman informed me, on the authority of a man from Banu Salul, He called his people to know him, and they chose him for that, but he refused and declined, so he went to Abdullah bin Amr and consulted with him. He consulted him and said: You do not know them. So they came in the morning and did not stop until they forced them to do so. So he went to Abdullah. Ibn Amr told him that he had been forced to do so, and he said: The beginning of it is intercession, the middle of it is betrayal, and the end of it is the torment of the Fire."
"27253","(27253) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ghalib, who said: We were sitting when a man entered and said: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, that the Prophet prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Whoever initiates a greeting to a people, bestows upon them ten good deeds, and says: My father sent me to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And peace be upon him, and he said: Come to him and say your greetings to him, and say to him: He is asking you to perform fortune-telling for him afterward. He said: Fortune-telling is true, fortune-telling is true, and there must be fortune-tellers, but the one who knows your station is ugly. (Abu Dawud 5189) Bazzar 808)"
"27254","(27254) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Qurayh narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: Abu Al-Sawwar said: By God I wish that your gaze in my lap was the place of fortune-telling."
"27255","(27255) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Salam bin Miskin narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Wasi’, on the authority of Al-Mahri, on the authority of Abu Harry said: He said to me: O Mary, do not be a tax collector, nor a foreman, nor a policeman."
"27256","(27256) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Ubaidah was the commoner of his people."
"27257","(27257) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, who said: Abu Al-Sawwar was an oracle in the time of Al-Hajjaj."
"27258","(27258) Ghassan bin Mudar narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Jabir, who said: When Omar became the ruler He imposed the religious duties, wrote down the collections of books, and introduced the scholars. Jabir said: So he introduced me to my companions."
"27259","(27259) Al-Fadl narrated to us, saying: Yunus bin Abi Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I saw Saeed bin Wahhab, and he was the commoner of his people."
"27260","(27260) Marhoum bin Abdul Aziz narrated to us, on the authority of his father: Abu Al-Sawwar was the chief of Banu Adiy."
"27261","Abu Abd al-Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shayba al-Absi narrated to us. He said:\n(27261) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling for a man. Of the Ansar, a master of Banu Adi killed him for blood money, twelve thousand, and about them was revealed: “And they did not take revenge except that God enriched them.” And His Messenger of His bounty}"
"27262","(27262) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ayyub ibn Musa, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, died. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him and his parents, the amount was eight hundred dinars, so Omar feared who would come after him, so he gave it twelve thousand dirhams, or a thousand. dinar"
"27263","(27263) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Layla told us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ubayd Al-Salmani, he said: Omar put He imposed on the people of gold a thousand dinars, and on the people of paper ten thousand, and on the people of camels a hundred camels, and on The people of cows are two hundred old cows, the people of sheep are two thousand sheep, and the people of livestock are two hundred camels."
"27264","(27264) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Ata’; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, imposed blood money on the people from their wealth, as long as it was: the owners of camels owed a hundred camels. And upon the people of the sheep are two thousand sheep, and upon the people of the cows are two hundred cows, and upon the people of the baruds are two hundred camels. He said: He has made There is something about those who eat food that I do not remember. (Abu Dawud 4531)"
"27265","(27265) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, who said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to the commanders of the soldiers: The blood money During the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, there were a hundred camels."
"27266","(27266) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The mistake is one hundred camels, so whoever adds a camel is a matter of the ignorant."
"27267","(27267) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; He made the blood money a hundred camels, and each camel was equal to a hundred, whether it had grown or grown small, so the people took it."
"27268","(27268) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah, and Zaid; They said: The blood money is one hundred camels."
"27269","(27269) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I praise Every twelve days, say a thousand glorifications, according to your religion, or he said: the value of your religion."
"27270","(27270) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Amr bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ikrimah; Omar ibn al-Khattab decreed blood money for the people of al-Quriya, twelve thousand, and said: “Times will change, and I fear for you.” The rulers after me, the people of the village are not obligated to impose any burden on their mind, nor the sacred month, nor the sanctuary, nor the mind. The people of the villages are harsh, not too much."
"27271","(27271) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; He led a man from Banu Mudlij who killed his son, so Omar took from him a hundred camels: thirty camels and thirty trunks. And forty successors."
"27272","(27272) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Zayd bin Jud’an, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Rabi’a, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivered a speech on the day of the conquest of Mecca, and he stood on the stairs. Al-Ka’bah, and he said: Praise be to God who fulfilled His promise, supported His servant, and defeated the parties alone. Indeed, the one who was killed intentionally A mistake with a whip or a stick contains a large amount of blood money: a hundred camels, forty calves, with their children in their bellies. (Abu Dawud 4536. Ahmed 11)"
"27273","(27273) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the teeth of camels in blood money, he said: Thirty calves, thirty Jad`a, twenty sons of Makhad, and twenty sons of Mukhadd. Laboun."
"27274","(27274) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, who said: Al-Zuhri used to say: Two hundred cows, or two thousand sheep."
"27275","(27275) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Bashir bin Yasar, on the authority of Sahil bin Abi Ḍṭṭma; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, paid tribute to a man with a hundred camels. (Bukhari 6898, Muslim 1291)"
"27276","(27276) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: A hundred camels, or two hundred camels. Others"
"27277","(27277) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, who said: The people of the camels give their camels. The people of cows are cows, the people of sheep are sheep, and the people of paper are paper."
"27278","(27278) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Omar and Uthman settled the blood money and left it to the giver. If he wanted, then camels, and if he wanted, then the money."
"27279","(27279) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, that Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: If the one who afflicted him was a Bedouin, Your ransom is a hundred camels. The Bedouin does not charge gold or paper. The blood money for a Bedouin if the Bedouin kills him is a hundred Camels. If the wise woman does not find any camels, then he should give her the equivalent of two thousand sheep."
"27280","(27280) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father said: They are given from whatever kind it is. The value of camels at that time was whatever it was, even if it increased, and if it decreased, then their value was."
"27281","(27281) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: I said to Ata’: If Al-Qarawi wants, he can give him a hundred camels, or Two hundred cows, or two thousand sheep, and he did not give any gold? He said: If he wishes, he can give you camels but not gold.\n He said: And Ataa said: It used to be said: On the people of camels are camels, and on the people of cows are cows, and on the people of sheep is a sheep."
"27282","(27282) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abd al-Karim bin Abi al-Mukhariq told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, He said: If the owner of cows and goats wishes, he can give him camels."
"27283","(27283) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr said: Who was His mind is in the matter, so each camel is worth twenty sheep, and whoever’s mind is cows, then every camel is worth two cows."
"27284","(27284) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Zayd bin Jubayr, on the authority of Khashf, on the authority of Abd God, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: Diyah is divided into fifths: twenty true, and twenty jud’. And twenty daughters of Labun, and twenty sons of Labun, and twenty daughters of Makhad. (Tirmidhi 1386. Daraqutni 175)"
"27285","(27285) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Qays, on the authority of Abdullah that He said: There are five sins: twenty Haqqa, twenty Jada’, twenty Banat Makhad, twenty Banu Makhad, and twenty Banat. Laboun."
"27286","(27286) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, the same."
"27287","(27287) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Sufyan. On the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ali, he said: He used to say in error four quarters: twenty-five rights, and five twenty-five of Jadah, twenty-five of the sons of Labun, and twenty-five of the daughters of Madhad."
"27288","(27288) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, and Abdullah, that they said: The error is in fifths."
"27289","(27289) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu Ayyad, on the authority of Uthman and Zayd, who said: In the error are thirty Jadiya, thirty daughters of Labun, and twenty sons of Labun. Twenty of the daughters of Makhad."
"27290","(27290) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Salih, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zaid; In the religion of error: thirty Jadiyah, thirty Haqqa, twenty Banu Labun, and twenty Banat Makhad."
"27291","(27291) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The diyah is divided by five-fifths."
"27292","(27292) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Alqamiya, and Al-Aswad, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: It is similar to intentional Arbaa: twenty-five Haqqah, twenty-five Jad`ah, twenty-five Banat Madhad, and twenty-five Banat Labun."
"27293","(27293) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Ibn Masoud used to say: In the likeness of The pillars are quarters: twenty-five jadha`, twenty-five haqqa, twenty-five banat labun, and twenty-five banat makhad."
"27294","(27294) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Omar; He said: In the shape of the pillars there are thirty trunks, thirty sockets, and forty between two and a half to Basel. All of them are behind you."
"27295","(27295) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: There are thirty-three pillars in the form of pillars. Haqqa, thirty-three Jud’ahs, and thirty-four Thanais to Basil al-Amha, all of them as successors."
"27296","(27296) Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab (h) and on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Abu Ayad; Othman and Zayd bin Thabit said: In the thick ones there are forty male offspring, thirty males, and thirty daughters. Laboun."
"27297","(27297) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, he said: Abu Musa and Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’abi used to say: In the heaviest portion of the blood money, there are thirty haqa’s, thirty jam’a’s, and forty thaniyyahs until Basil for the entire year. successor"
"27298","(27298) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Abi Khaled told us, on the authority of Amer, he said: Zayd bin Thabit used to say: In Shabab columns: thirty ḍqāqā, thirty ḍādī, and forty between two and ḍāl, all of them successive,\n And Ali used to say: Concerning the shape of the pillars: thirty-three Ḍaqqīs, thirty-three ḍādīs, and thirty-four mas Between then and now, to Basel, all of them behind him."
"27299","(27299) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us?? On the authority of Ash'ath, on the authority of Amir, Al-Hasan, Ibn Sirin, and Amr ibn Dinar, they said: The shape of pillars makes the religion heavy for them. In the teeth of camels."
"27300","(27300) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is almost intentional. ; Striking with a piece of wood, or throwing a large stone, the blood money is in three parts: a third of a hqaq, a third of a jud`a, and a third of what is in between. Then go to Basel every year after you."
"27301","(27301) Muhammad Ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, who said: Ata’ said: The blood money is made heavy in cases of premeditation, and there is no He will be killed with it."
"27302","(27302) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: How thick are camels? He said: Forty successors, thirty right ones, and thirty jud’ahs."
"27303","(27303) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In Al-Taghlidh: Forty Thaniyah until Basel, all of them as successors, thirty Haqqiyah, and thirty Bint Makhad."
"27304","(27304) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Excessiveness in resemblance to the teeth of camels."
"27305","(27305) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: He likened the pillars to a great stone. And the stick."
"27306","(27306) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: the one killed by the whip and the stick, almost intentionally. (Abu Dawud 4535. Ahmed 164)"
"27307","(27307) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Hakam, and Hammad, who said: He was not struck by a stone, or A whip, or a stick, which fell upon the soul, so it is like an intentional act, and it contains heavy blood money."
"27308","(27308) Wakī’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiră, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The likeness of intentionality is everything. He is baptized with it without iron, and there is no resemblance to baptism except in the soul, and it is not without the soul."
"27309","(27309) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There was no killing without a weapon, then it was similar. Intentionally, the blood money is required by the wise one."
"27310","(27310) Muhammad bin Musab told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: It is similar to intentionality when a man hits another man in the The revenge is between them, and he does not want to kill him, so he gets sick from that and dies."
"27311","(27311) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Aazib, on the authority of Al-Numan bin Bashir, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Everything is a mistake except the sword, and for every mistake there is an arrow.\n(Ahmad 275. Bazzar 3244)"
"27312","(27312) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The mistake is to want something. Then you infect others."
"27313","(27313) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The mistake is if you strike a human being and do not want it, so that is upon you. The wise one"
"27314","(27314) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hamza Al-Asadi, who said: I witnessed a shariah who made a judgment in Muddhihi for five hundred percent. Dirham"
"27315","(27315) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hakim bin Al-Daylam, he said: I came with an explanation in clarification. He decided on it with five short sentences."
"27316","(27316) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Shaybah bin Musawar, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling on five camels in al-Muddahah, and he did not make a ruling on anything else except that.\n(Abdul Razzaq 17316)"
"27317","(27317) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather. ; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided five times in the clarification. (Abu Dawud 4555. Tirmidhi 1390)"
"27318","(27318) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling on five camels in al-Muddahah, and he did not make a ruling on anything else except that."
"27319","(27319) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, judged the matter of the Muddahiyah and onward, so he placed five camels in the Mudhahiyah."
"27320","(27320) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: In Al-Mudhīḥ there are five Camels"
"27321","(27321) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, he said: In Al-Mudhiyah Five camels."
"27322","(2732) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, on the authority of Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz, who said: It contains five of Camels"
"27323","(27323) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In the clarification of the verse there are five obligatory duties."
"27324","(27324) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amr, on the authority of Omar ibn Abdul Aziz, who said: In al-Muddahiya there are five camels, Or something made of gold or paper."
"27325","(27325) Yahya bin Abdul-Malik bin Abi Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, saying: In The explanation is five camels."
"27326","(27326) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: In the clarification book there are five camels."
"27327","(27327) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: Husayn al-Mu’allim informed us, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of His grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are five things in the clarification. (Abu Dawud 455. Tirmidhi 1390)"
"27328","(27328) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Umar, who said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are five things in the clarification."
"27329","(27329) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, he said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote: Not to add anything to the clarifier. Fifty dinars. Khaled said: He wants the clarification in the face."
"27330","(27330) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: In al-Mudhihi there are five camels."
"27331","(27331) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: In Al-Muddahiya there are five camels divided into quarters: A quarter of Jad`ah, a quarter of Haqqaq, a quarter of the daughters of Labun, and a quarter of the daughters of Madhad."
"27332","(27332) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Aamir, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the clarification, five camels are five-fifths."
"27333","(27333) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, and Shurayh; They said: In the clarification there are five camels: Haqqa, Jad`a, Bint Madhad, Bint Labun, and Ibn Labun."
"27334","(27334) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; In Al-Sunnah and Al-Muddhahi there are five camels: Ibn Makhad; A female and a male, and the sons of Labun, and Jadha`ah, and Haqqiyah."
"27335","(27335) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In Diyah Al-Muddahhih: Bint Makhad, Ibn Labun, Ibn Labun, Haqqiyah, and Jad`iyah."
"27336","(27336) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhul (h) and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed a third of the blood money for the slave women. (Abu Dawud 257. An-Nasa’i 7060)"
"27337","(27337) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: A third of the blood money is due in the motherhood."
"27338","(27338) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the mother’s debt is a third of the blood money in fifths."
"27339","(27339) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A third of the blood money is due in the slave labor."
"27340","(27340) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A third of the blood money is due in the motherhood."
"27341","(27341) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: A third of the blood money is due in the motherhood."
"27342","(27342) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of al-Dahhak, who said: A third of the blood money is for the slaves."
"27343","(27343) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; The third part of the mother’s prayer."
"27344","(27344) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; Shurayh judged the people of four thousand people."
"27345","(27345) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: In Al-Munqilah there are fifteen."
"27346","(27346) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Umar, who narrated it, and he said: There are fifteen times in Al-Manqilah."
"27347","(27347) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In Al-Munqilah there are fifteen camels, Or something made of gold or paper."
"27348","(27348) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There are fifteen things in Al-Munqilah."
"27349","(27349) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There are fifteen times in Al-Munqīlah."
"27350","(27350) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, who said: There are fifteen in it."
"27351","(27351) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In Al-Munqilah there are fifteen Fifths."
"27352","(27352) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, who said: In Al-Munqilah there are fifteen camels in quarters. : A quarter of Jad`a, a quarter of Haqqaq, a quarter of the Banat Labun, and a quarter of the Banat Makhad."
"27353","(27353) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled in The movable number is fifteen."
"27354","(27354) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali used to make things that had not been made clear and were almost Four camels."
"27355","(27355) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; In Al-Simhaq: four camels, and something similar was mentioned on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali."
"27356","(27356) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Yazid ibn Abdullah ibn Qusayt, On the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, that Omar and Othman made a judgment in the court, and Al-Simhaq was half of the Muddahiyah’s blood money."
"27357","(27357) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever is less than the clarification includes reconciliation."
"27358","(27358) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amir, who said: He said: What is less than the clarification is the reward of a doctor."
"27359","(27359) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimoon, who said: Umar ibn Abd al-Aziz wrote: Not among them. Without the clarification there is no reason except the reward of the doctor."
"27360","(27360) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is a ruling regarding what is less than what is explained."
"27361","(27361) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is nothing in it except what is clarified. Doctor's reward."
"27362","(27362) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the scratch, or the thing? He said: He made peace, as long as he did not reach an obligatory period."
"27363","(27363) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: Al-Hasan did not specify anything other than the clarifier."
"27364","(27364) Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Asadi told us, on the authority of Ibn Ulathah, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Abi Ablah; Muadh and Omar gave the reward of a doctor to something less than al-Muddahhi."
"27365","(27365) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; Abu Bakr and Omar said: The one who makes it clear is the same in the face and the head."
"27366","(27366) Abdou bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Amr bin Maimun, that Omar bin Abd al-Aziz wrote: That the clarifier in The face and head are the same, and there are five camels in it."
"27367","(27367) Yahya bin Saeed Al-Qattan narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, he said: Al-Muddhiha On the face is the same as the one on the head, except that there is an appearance on the face, in which case it should be as much as that until it reaches half the length of the face. The mind of the clarifier"
"27368","(27368) Abdullah bin Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The clarifier is in the face and the head."
"27369","(27369) Hatim bin Wardan narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The one that is cleaned in the face and the head are the same, except that There is a shine on the face, so it increases the amount of shame."
"27370","(27370) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid, who said: The one who makes clear is in the face, the head, and the nose. Either way"
"27371","(27371) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The clarifier is in the head and the face. Either way"
"27372","(2737) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The one that is made clear on the face is like the one that is made clear on the head."
"27373","(27373) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Shurayh, and Al-Hasan, who said: The one who is clear on the face is like The clarification is in the head."
"27374","(27374) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hamran, on the authority of Iyas bin Mu’awiyah, who said: Al-Mudhihi is the same as here and here. Mu`tamir pointed with his hand towards his head and face."
"27375","(27375) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders; Omar bin Abdul Aziz said: Five by five."
"27376","(27376) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, he said: The ones that are explained in the head are five, And in the face there are ten."
"27377","(27377) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer, who said: The one that is made clear in the face has two religions."
"27378","(27378) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the ear is half the blood money."
"27379","(27379) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zayd, who said: If the ear rings, then there is Detita"
"27380","(27380) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Abu Bakr said: In The ear is fifteen because it does not harm its hearing, and hair and turban cover it."
"27381","(27381) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to say: In the ear when fifty camels are removed."
"27382","(27382) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: In the ear when fifty camels are removed."
"27383","(27383) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me that there is a letter by Omar Ibn Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, said: In the ear is half the blood money, or the equivalent of that in gold."
"27384","(27384) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Bakr, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: In the ear is half the blood money."
"27385","(27385) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the ear, if half of it is removed The money is paid in fifths, so whatever is short of it will be accounted for."
"27386","(27386) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Omar, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: In the nose, if the blood clot is removed, it will be removed."
"27387","(27387) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the bloody nose."
"27388","(27388) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the nose is blood money, and whatever is cut off from the nose there will be a reckoning."
"27389","(27389) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: It was in The letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Amr bin Hazm: In the nose, if the blood is absorbed, it will be marna."
"27390","(27390) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In the nose is blood, and it is not diminished. From the nose, then by its reckoning."
"27391","(27391) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The nose and the ear are in the same position as the tooth, so long as it is lacking. So with reckoning."
"27392","(27392) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; In the nose, if its stump is cut, or the marn is cut, the blood money is divided into fifths, and whatever is reduced from it is to be reckoned."
"27393","(27393) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: In the dung is a third The blood money. If the deceased reaches the bone, then he must pay the blood money. If he gets some of the droppings of a rabbit or something else, unless When the bone is reached, it is calculated as dung."
"27394","(27394) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Suleiman bin Musa said: Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote To the commanders of the soldiers: In the nose, when a goat is given full blood money, and whatever is struck on the nose will be taken into account."
"27395","(27395) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: In the two goats is the blood money."
"27396","(27396) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: In the land of blood."
"27397","(27397) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, he said: In the nose is blood."
"27398","(27398) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: In the rabbit is a third of the blood money. And in Witr is a third of the blood money."
"27399","(27399) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, and Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: In The three holes in the nose are blood money, and in each one is a third of the blood money."
"27400","(27400) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: In dung A third of the blood money, and if it comes from rabbit dung or something else unless it reaches the bone, then it will be paid for."
"27401","(27401) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is there a hollow in the nose? He said: Yes."
"27402","(27402) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; He used to say: In the nasal cavity is a third of the blood money, and if he pays it, then two-thirds."
"27403","(27403) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Saeed bin Masruq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man who broke another man's nose, and Ali Uthman was healed? He said: There is a ruling on it."
"27404","(27404) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Othman bin Abi Sulayman informed me; A mamluk of Jubair ibn Abi Sulaiman broke one of the bridges in the nose of a servant of Ata’ ibn Bakht, and that Ibn Suraqah Omar bin Abdul Aziz asked about that? Then Omar said: We found in a book by Omar Ibn Al-Khattab: Whichever bone is broken and then repaired as it was, it contains two truths. So Ibn Omar was robbed, and he said: One of the two reeds was broken, so Omar refused except to put two pieces of water in it and fulfill it."
"27405","(27405) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ammarah, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Amr bin Hazm, he said: In The letter of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Amr bin Hazm: And in the eye are fifty."
"27406","(27406) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the spring is half The blood money"
"27407","(27407) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Omar, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are fifty in the eye."
"27408","(27408) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: The spring is fifty."
"27409","(27409) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the eye is half the blood money, Fifths."
"27410","(27410) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In the eye is half the blood money."
"27411","(27411) Abdullah bin Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; On the eyebrows when they are cut off, the blood money is paid, and on one of them is half the blood money."
"27412","(27412) Abu Bakr bin Ayash and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Concerning the eyebrows The blood money"
"27413","(27413) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In the two eyebrows is blood money, and in one of them is half. The blood money"
"27414","(27414) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr made a ruling in the case of Hajj. If he is afflicted, his hair will fall out with two explanations: Ten camels."
"27415","(27415) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: One-third of the eyebrows. The blood money"
"27416","(27416) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: In every two men And the woman who has blood money; The hands and the eyebrows, and Al-Sha’bi said: Every human being has two blood money."
"27417","(27417) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abd al-Karim bin Abi al-Mukhariq informed me; He reported it on the authority of some of the Prophet’s companions, may God bless him and grant him peace. That in the eyebrow, the hairs are matted; For in it all is a quarter, and whatever is gone of it, there will be a reckoning."
"27418","(27418) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: What was Two of the human beings are the blood money, and each one of them bears half the blood money, and if there is one person, the blood money is in it for each one of them."
"27419","(27419) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Minhal bin Khalifa Al-Ijlili narrated to us, on the authority of Salma bin Tammam Al-Shaqri, who said: A man passed by With a pot, and it fell on a man’s head and burned his hair. He was raised to a high place, and he postponed it for a year, but it did not grow, so he judged it. Ali with the blood money."
"27420","(27420) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; Concerning the hair, if it does not grow then the blood money."
"27421","(27421) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Muslim, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It contains blood money."
"27422","(27422) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Is shaving the head a vowel? He means Arsha. He said: I did not know."
"27423","(27423) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid, who said: On the upper blade is half the blood money. And in the lower blade is a third of the blood money."
"27424","(27424) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Bayan Abi Bishr, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, he said: They did not set the time in The labia are something."
"27425","(27425) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Among the Shifar are blood money, and in each of them is a quarter. The blood money"
"27426","(27426) Issa bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: For each shoulder blade there is a quarter of the blood money."
"27427","(27427) Shababă told us, on the authority of Shu`bā, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Shubarmā, who said: Abraham used to say: In the lips. Ruling by people of justice."
"27428","(27428) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me; Omar bin Abdulaziz wrote to the commanders of the soldiers: On the upper blade of the eye: When half the blood money is taken, and on the lower blade: A third of the blood money."
"27429","(27429) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, he said: In the lower eyelid there are two thirds, and in the upper one a third."
"27430","(27430) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: In the eyelids, in each eyelid is a quarter of the blood money."
"27431","(27431) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: They used to put it on my eyelids. The eye when the blood money is removed from the eye, and that is because there is no remnant of the eye after them, so if they separate, they put in the bottom third. And at the top there are two-thirds, and that is because it is more severe from the eye than the lower part, it covers and protects from it."
"27432","(27432) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to the commanders of the soldiers: that they write to him with the knowledge of their scholars, and it was from what was gathered The commanders of the soldiers are required to pay: If the drinker smeared his hair, then there are sixty dinars, and if he smeared all of his hair, then there are one hundred and twenty dinars."
"27433","(27433) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: They used to put it in the mouth when it split. The blood money"
"27434","(27434) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: If a man is beaten until His hearing is gone, and blood money is in it."
"27435","(27435) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who was beaten and lost his hearing, sight and speech. He said to him: Three blood money."
"27436","(27436) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: I heard a sheikh say before Ibn al-Ash’ath’s trial, so I described his description, and they said: That’s it. Abu Al-Muhallab, the uncle of Abu Qalabab, said: A man threw a stone at his head, and his hearing, his tongue, his mind, and his memory were gone. He did not have sexual intercourse with women, so Umar paid four blood money for her."
"27437","(27437) Omar bin Yunus narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: In the eternal hearing."
"27438","(27438) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: In The disappearance of hearing is fifty."
"27439","(27439) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ about a man who was injured in one of his extremities, what was his fate? More than his blood money? He said: I have not heard of anything concerning him, and I think he will be given whatever he was afflicted with, even if it is more than His name"
"27440","(27440) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ibn Shihab said about a man who gouged out his companion’s eye and cut out his eye. His nose and his ears. He said: All of that counts."
"27441","(27441) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; Al-Hasan was asked about a man who threw a stone, or was hit on the head, and his hearing and sight went away, and his senses were cut off? He said: Blood money. In his hearing there is corruption, in his sight there is corruption in his tongue, and it was said to Al-Hasan: He won, and he said: By God, he did not win. And he did not succeed."
"27442","(27442) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I was informed that a man came to him, Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He said: So-and-so hit me until one of my ears became deaf, so he said: How do we know? He said: Call the doctors, so they called them and they smelled her, and they said: This is the deaf woman."
"27443","(27443) Omar bin Ali bin Ata bin Muqaddam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit; Concerning the man who claims that his hearing has disappeared, he said: He swears on it."
"27444","(27444) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Shurayh; That a man claimed that his hearing had disappeared; So he ordered that he be sworn to him."
"27445","(27445) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; About a man who claimed that his hearing had disappeared? He said: It is looked at by those who know it, meaning doctors."
"27446","(27446) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he heard thunder, he fainted. In it is the blood money."
"27447","(27447) Yahya ibn Yaman told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He wakes up and wakes up with it."
"27448","(27448) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Al-Zubayr ibn Junada narrated to us, saying: I asked Ata’ about a man who hit a man and he went away. He heard him, and he was all-hearing? He said: He should be left, and if he sleeps heavily, someone will be brought to him. If he does not wake up, then it is blood money, and if he wakes up, then it is blood money. Government"
"27449","(27449) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of someone who heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and he was asked about a man who struck his throat. A man, so his voice disappeared? He said: This is the blood money."
"27450","(27450) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid, who said: If a man is beaten, he hums, or sings, or laughs. For each one there is a blood money."
"27451","(27451) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar; The commanders of the soldiers gathered for Omar bin Abdul Aziz in the throat, and if it broke, the voice would be cut off from the man, the blood money. Completely"
"27452","(27452) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan: If his words disappear, then the blood money is due."
"27453","(27453) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid; In the blood clot"
"27454","(27454) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me: The commanders of the soldiers gathered According to Omar bin Abdul Aziz regarding Al-Zaar, if a man does not turn around except when he turns away: fifty dinars."
"27455","(27455) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; A man had an injury to another man's eye, so part of his sight was gone and some remained. So that matter was reported to Ali, so he ordered that his eye be cleaned. So she was tied up, and he ordered a man to bring some white ones, and he set off with them while he looked until his eyesight gave out, then he drew a flag at that time, saying: Then he looked into it and found it to be the same, so he said: So give him the amount of the other person’s wealth that he lost in his insight."
"27456","(27456) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who gouged out a man’s eye while he saw it, he said: He will be fined in proportion to what he reduced from it."
"27457","(27457) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: There are fifty in the eye. He said: Some of them went away. He saw it and some remained. He said: For the account of what he had gone. He said: He holds it according to the Sahih, so he looks at the other one, then he holds it. On the other, then he looks at the authentic one, and what is left of it is counted.\n I said: His eyes weakened from old age and became injured. He said: He vowed to her in full."
"27458","(27458) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ali’s statement was mentioned regarding what His eye was affected where he saw the white, so Al-Sha’bi said: If he wished, he could add to his eye with which he could see. He said: He sees with it more than he sees with it, and if he wishes, he can remove the damage from the eye that was damaged, so he said: No. He sees with it and he sees with it, but something more similar than that is for a doctor to look at what he sees and see what is missing. From us"
"27459","(27459) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid; On the lower lip is a third of the blood money, because it holds food and drink, and on the upper lip is a third of the blood money."
"27460","(27460) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; At the bottom is a third of the blood money, and at the top is a third of the blood money."
"27461","(27461) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, that he said: On the lips is blood; At the bottom is a third of the blood money, and at the top is a third of the blood money."
"27462","(27462) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: On the two lips is the blood money, and on one of them is half. The blood money"
"27463","(27463) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Shurayh; On the lips is blood money."
"27464","(27464) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Amir, who said: On the lips is blood money, and on each one of them. Half"
"27465","(27465) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: It was not of two In the case of a human being, the blood money is included in both of them, and in each of them is half the blood money, and if there is one of them, the blood money is in it."
"27466","(27466) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr decided on the lips. With blood money, a hundred camels."
"27467","(27467) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What is the matter with the lips? He said: Fifty camels, each one of them. I said: Is there better between them? He said: The lower ones are preferred, they claimed. I said: How much? He said: I don't know."
"27468","(27468) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, that He said: There are fifty in the lips, and the lower part is preferred over the upper part of men and women by being thick, and is not preferred by more. In number, but fifty means the teeth of a camel."
"27469","(27469) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The lips are equal; Half and half."
"27470","(27470) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: On the lips is the blood money, on the lower two-thirds, and in The highest third."
"27471","(27471) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Omar, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: In the tongue, the religion is complete."
"27472","(27472) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who narrated it, and said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: In the tongue when the blood money is collected in full."
"27473","(27473) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, who narrated it, like him."
"27474","(27474) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the old tongue."
"27475","(27475) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; In the tongue, if the blood money is taken back by fifths, then whatever is reduced will be accounted for."
"27476","(27476) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, he said: In the entire tongue, And whatever is afflicted with the tongue, and it reaches the level of preventing speech, then it is a full blood money."
"27477","(27477) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Concerning the knot of the tongue."
"27478","(27478) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, the same as him."
"27479","(27479) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: Concerning the tongue when it splits. Then twenty camels came together."
"27480","(27480) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: Should the entire tongue be cut off? He said: Blood money."
"27481","(27481) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq ruled on the tongue. If it is cut with blood money, if it is cut from its roots, and if its roots are cut and its owner speaks, then it is half of the blood money.\n(Bayhaqi 89)"
"27482","(27482) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Suleiman bin Musa said: In the book of Omar bin Abdul Aziz : Whatever is cut off from the tongue to the extent that it prevents all speech is blood money, and whatever is short of that is to be taken into account."
"27483","(27483) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me that there is a letter by Omar Bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Omar Bin Al-Khattab; With regard to the tongue, if the blood money is removed in its entirety, and whatever is affected on the tongue to the extent that it prevents speech, then it is the blood money in full. And on a woman’s tongue there is a complete blood-money, and whatever is afflicted on her tongue that reaches the point of preventing speech, then it is a complete blood-money. And whatever is less than that will be taken into account. (Abu Dawud 261)"
"27484","(27484) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the divine tongue."
"27485","(27485) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It is the blood money."
"27486","(27486) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar told me; The commanders of the soldiers gathered to pay Omar bin Abdul Aziz a third of the blood money."
"27487","(27487) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: He informed me on the authority of Al-Sha’bi that he said: Concerning the beard when it is broken. Forty dinars."
"27488","(27488) Muhammad ibn Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I narrated on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, that he said: In my mouth. A person bends his thumb, then places his lower reed, and opens his mouth, placing it between his jaws. Whatever is missing from the opening of his mouth from the lower reed of his thumb will be accounted for."
"27489","(27489) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Omar, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: There are fifty in hand. (Abu Dawud 4553. Ahmed 217)"
"27490","(27490) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Amara, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Amr ibn Hazm, he said: It was in A letter from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Amr bin Hazm: In hand are fifty. (Nasa’i 7059)"
"27491","(27491) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the hand is half The blood money"
"27492","(27492) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the hand is half the blood money, fifty of The camels are four quarters, one quarter Jada`, one quarter Haqqaq, one quarter the daughters of Labun, and one quarter the daughters of Makhad."
"27493","(27493) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the hand is half the blood money."
"27494","(27494) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the hand is half the money, in fifths."
"27495","(27495) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Hakim bin Hakim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said: It was While Abu Bakr and Omar put the issue in the wounds: the hand if its owner does not eat with it and does not cover himself, He did not like her, but her mind was perfect, so whatever was lacking was taken into account."
"27496","(27496) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ata’ said: With the hand you can uproot fifty. I said: Amen. From the shoulder, or from the shoulder? He said: No, but rather from the bent."
"27497","(27497) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the fingers are cut off The blood money, and if the hand is cut off, then fifty camels."
"27498","(27498) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If the hand is cut off at the joint, then in it Half the blood money, and if it is cut from the `udd, then half the blood money is due."
"27499","(27499) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Two hands are equal."
"27500","(27500) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the hand is cut from the joint, then it Dittata, and if any of it is cut off after that, then there is a just ruling, and if it is cut off from the upper arm, or the lower part of The forearm is a thing, for it is a sacrifice."
"27501","(27501) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What if the hand was cut off from half the arm? He said: Fifty. I said: So what was left after that was cut off? He said: A wound. I do not think anything other than that, unless it is Sunnah."
"27502","(27502) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: The palm of fifty camels is cut off, but if what remains of the whole hand, or the arm, or half the arm is cut off: then half a vow. The hand also, twenty-five, if it was only cut off from half of the arm, or the arm after the palm, Mujahid said: He says that, so half of the vow on the hand is cut off, and if all that remains is cut off, then a wound will be seen in it. (Abdul Razzaq 17689)"
"27503","(27503) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Muslim bin Jundub, on the authority of Aslam Mawla Omar, he said: I heard Omar saying on the pulpit: There is a camel in the collarbone."
"27504","(27504) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Jundub al-Qasas, on the authority of Aslam, the client of Omar; He made a ruling regarding a camel's clavicle."
"27505","(27505) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: In The collarbone is a camel."
"27506","(27506) Waki’ and Abu Khalid told us, on the authority of Shu’bai, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: In The collarbone with goats."
"27507","(27507) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: There is a ruling on clavicle."
"27508","(27508) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, and Al-Sha’abi; They said: If it is broken, then forty dinars."
"27509","(27509) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Karim informed me, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, he said : If the collarbone is cut off and he does not live, then he gets the full blood money, but if he lives, then fifty camels are paid for it."
"27510","(27510) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Hazim, on the authority of his leaders, who said: If the collarbone is forced, then there are four Abharaa, meaning a proverb of immorality."
"27511","(27511) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled on A tooth equals five camels.\n He said: And my father said: Some of them are preferred over others, according to the opinion of the people of opinion and counsel. (Abu Dawud 261, Abdul Razzaq 17490)"
"27512","(27512) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abi Aroub narrated to us, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of His father, on the authority of his grandfather; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In the teeth, five by five. \n(Abu Dawud 4553. Ahmed 182)"
"27513","(27513) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn al-Mu’allim, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Five years in age. (Abu Dawud 4552. An-Nasa’i 7045)"
"27514","(27514) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In the tooth is five camels, or This is made of gold or paper."
"27515","(27515) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Dawud ibn Husayn, on the authority of Abu Ghatafan al-Marri, on the authority of Ibn Abbas He said: The teeth are perfect. Count it with your fingers."
"27516","(27516) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuḥayl, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: The teeth are equal."
"27517","(27517) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: Urwa al-Bariqi came to me from Omar: The fingers and teeth in blood money are equal."
"27518","(27518) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Teeth are equal, and he said: If the dual has beauty, then The molar has a benefit."
"27519","(27519) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: It is the same."
"27520","(27520) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The blood money is equal."
"27521","(27521) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, who said: I bear witness to Shurayh and Masruq that they are They made the fingers and teeth equal in blood money."
"27522","(27522) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, who said: A tooth includes five camels."
"27523","(27523) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, he said: Ikrimah bin Khalid narrated to us, on the authority of a man from the family of Umar; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed a ruling on the death of five camels."
"27524","(27524) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Suleiman bin Musa informed me; In the letter of Omar bin Abdul Aziz to the commanders of the soldiers: And in the teeth are five camels."
"27525","(27525) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In the tooth, five camels are five-fifths."
"27526","(27526) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Teeth are straight."
"27527","(27527) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In the teeth, five by five."
"27528","(27528) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Ataa said to me: Concerning the two- and four-sided teeth, And the two canine teeth were five by five, and while what remained was two claws, the top of the mouth and the bottom of it were the same, in two folds. And four quadrants, and the canines at the top and bottom of the mouth are the same, and the molars at the top of the mouth are the same, and the molars at the bottom of the mouth are the same."
"27529","(27529) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid; Like the saying of Ataa, he said: The teeth from the top and bottom of the mouth, and the molars from the top and bottom of the mouth, are the same."
"27530","(27530) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father said: Some of them are preferred over others, according to what the people of Opinion and advice."
"27531","(27531) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Amr bin Muslim informed me; He heard a peacock saying: The six at the top and bottom of the mouth are better than the molars. And he said: In the molars are young camels."
"27532","(27532) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Omar ibn al-Khattab made a decree on what came from the mouth of five obligatory prayers, and that is fifty dinars, the value of each obligatory prayer. Ten dinars, and in the molars there is a camel.\n Yahya mentioned: What comes before the mouth; Two-sided, four-sided, and two-sided ones.\n Sa`id said: Even when he was with Mu'awiyah and his molars were affected, he said: I am more knowledgeable about molars than Omar, so he made up for it five days. Obligations"
"27533","(27533) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace May God bless him and grant him peace: This and that are the same, meaning the little finger and the thumb. (Bukhari 6895, Abu Dawud 4546)"
"27534","(27534) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Shurayh said: Urwiy al-Bariqi came to me from Omar: The fingers in the blood are equal."
"27535","(27535) Abu Khalid Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit, who said: The fingers are equal."
"27536","(27536) Abu Khaled and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He said: It is the same."
"27537","(27537) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Blood money is equal on the fingers."
"27538","(27538) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, he said: I found in my book on the authority of Humayd, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Hisham bin"
"27539","(27539) Hafs bin Ghayath and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Sha’biy, who said: I bear witness to Sharih and stolen. Indeed, they made the fingers and teeth equal."
"27540","(27540) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: The fingers are equal, ten by ten."
"27541","(27541) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ghalib al-Tamar, on the authority of Masruq bin Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: There are ten fingers in ten. (Abu Dawud 4545. Ahmed 397)"
"27542","(27542) Muhammad bin Bishr and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Ghalib al-Tamar, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, on the authority of Masruq Bin Aws, on the authority of Abu Musa; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling on ten camels. (Abu Dawud 4544, Ibn Majah 2654)"
"27543","(27543) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Matar, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided on the fingers: ten by ten. (Abu Dawud 4551, Ahmed 215)"
"27544","(27544) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ikrimah ibn Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Umar, who said: The Messenger said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: On each of your fingers there are ten camels."
"27545","(27545) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: On the fingers, on every finger. A tenth of the blood money"
"27546","(27546) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the finger is a tenth of blood money."
"27547","(27547) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; For every toe there is a camel's tenth, or something of gold or paper."
"27548","(27548) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; On each finger is one-fifth of the blood money."
"27549","(27549) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: All fingers are equal. It contains the tithe."
"27550","(27550) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There are ten obligatory duties for every finger."
"27551","(27551) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a judgment regarding each finger. From what you get is a tenth of the blood money."
"27552","(27552) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Omar decreed half of the palm of the palm of your thumb and the one next to your palm, and ten obligatory prayers for the middle, and the next With nine obligatory prayers, and on the little finger with six obligatory prayers."
"27553","(27553) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad, who said: The fingers are ten, ten."
"27554","(27554) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ali, Ibn Masoud, Ibn Abbas, and Al-Hasan, They used to say: There are ten in all of the fingers."
"27555","(27555) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Khaled Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Abu Qalaba, on the authority of Amr bin Salama, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan wrote to us, while we were with Khaled ibn Abdullah, saying that the fingers were three, and Khaled was joined between the little finger. And the ring finger, and between the middle and the next, and the thumb on one side."
"27556","(27556) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In each joint of the fingers, a third The blood of a finger, except for the thumb, for in each joint there is half the blood."
"27557","(27557) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: There are fifteen in the thumb, and in The next one is ten, and the next is ten, and the next is eight, and the next is seven."
"27558","(27558) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Zaid; He said: In the fingers, each joint is a third of the finger’s blood money, except for the thumb, for in it is half the blood money if It was cut from the joint, because it had two joints."
"27559","(27559) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; The portion of the fingers on the hands and feet amounted to ten camels."
"27560","(27560) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; That Hisham bin Hubaira wrote to Shurayh asking him, so he wrote to him: The fingers of the feet and the hands Either way"
"27561","(27561) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The fingers of both hands and toes are equal."
"27562","(27562) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The fingers of two hands And the two feet are equal."
"27563","(27563) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz; That a man asked Ibn Omar about the one-eyed person whose eye should be gouged out? Abdullah bin Safwan said: Omar paid blood money on her."
"27564","(27564) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abd Rabbah, on the authority of Abu Ayyad; Othman died in one eye, and the entire eye of the healthy and blood-redeemed man was injured."
"27565","(27565) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; Concerning a one-eyed man, if his healthy eye is injured, he says: If he wishes, an eye can be gouged out in place of another, and he can take half, and if If he wishes, he can take the full blood money."
"27566","(27546) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: If the eye of the one-eyed person is gouged out It is a complete blood money."
"27567","(27567) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Lahiq bin Hamid; Did he ask Ibn Umar, or did a man ask him about the one-eyed man whose healthy eye was gouged out? Ibn Safwan said, while he was with Ibn Omar: A lifetime had paid a full blood money on her, so he said: I am only asking you, O Ibn Omar, He said: Are you asking me? This tells you that Omar has completely paid off the blood money on her. (Bayhaqi 94)"
"27568","(27568) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He mentioned what they say about a one-eyed man if his right eye is gouged out, and he does not take a bribe for the other. They said: The full blood money. Ibrahim said: Some people from Banu Kahil claimed that this was their case, so Uthman ruled on it. This is the fault of both eyes, so we asked about the hidden meaning of that, so we searched for it, but we did not find an outlet for it, so it became cold."
"27569","(27569) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In the spring if no one remains. He changed her eyesight, then she was injured, the full blood money."
"27570","(27570) Yazid told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; In one-eyed man whose eye was gouged out. He said: In her is the full blood money."
"27571","(27571) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh; He said: Concerning a man whose eye is gouged out, and he has no other eye. He said: Retaliation, and if it is gouged out by mistake, then half. The blood money"
"27572","(27572) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Masruq; In the one-eyed man, his healthy eye is put out. He said: In it is half. Shall I perform the sacrifice for the one killed by God?"
"27573","(27573) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman and Waki` told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of al-Sha`bi; In the one-eyed person, the healthy eye is deliberately gouged out. He said: An eye for an eye."
"27574","(27574) Waki’ and Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Abi Ad-Duha, on the authority of Abd Allah bin fool; In the case of a one-eyed person, his healthy eye is intentionally gouged out. He said: An eye for an eye. I did not go out his first eye."
"27575","(27575) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Abi Rabah, he said: It contains half. The blood money"
"27576","(27576) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It contains half the blood money."
"27577","(27577) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amer, on the authority of Masruq; He was asked about a one-eyed man whose eye was gouged out? He said: I will not pay the blood money to the one who was killed by God, but the one who afflicted it must pay the blood money for one eye."
"27578","(27578) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Amer; Concerning one-eyed man, he gouged out the eye of a man and said: An eye for an eye."
"27579","(27579) Gandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the one-eyed man, if he gouges out the eye of a man, his eye will be gouged out."
"27580","(27580) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: An eye for an eye."
"27581","(27581) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid, (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (H) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a tooth becomes black, it will be cleaned."
"27582","(27582) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zayd, (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husain al-Harithi, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali (H), on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"27583","(27583) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: If the tooth turns black, clean it. Completely"
"27584","(27584) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: If she turns black, her mind is perfect."
"27585","(27585) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh; If a tooth turned black, he would make up for it."
"27586","(27586) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He said: If a tooth becomes black, or moves, or trembles, then it is equal."
"27587","(27587) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Al-Qasim; The tooth was trembling. He said: Her mind is perfect."
"27588","(27588) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the tooth turns black or becomes yellow, then there is a blood money in it."
"27589","(27589) Zayd bin Al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If the tooth turns black, then it has been cleaned."
"27590","(27590) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; In old age, it should be used with care. If it turns black, then the mind is perfect."
"27591","(27591) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He lurks around her all the time."
"27592","(27592) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid; Like him"
"27593","(27593) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham; Like him"
"27594","(27594) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Regarding the age, one can use it for a year."
"27595","(27595) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning age, he said: He is waiting for it for a long time."
"27596","(27596) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: If a tooth is broken, he will postpone it for another year."
"27597","(27597) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He should wait for a tooth with it, if it turns black, or It turned yellow, and within it was the mind."
"27598","(27598) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali; In the case of a tooth, if some of it is broken, its owner will be given compensation in exchange for what was missing from it."
"27599","(27599) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"27600","(27600) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, (H) On the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid, (h) And on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Like him"
"27601","(27601) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The nose and the ear are in the same position as the tooth, so long as it is lacking. So with reckoning."
"27602","(27602) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz; There are five camels in the tooth, and if any of them is broken, if it is not black, then there will be a reckoning."
"27603","(27603) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar and Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh; He used to add to it the same amount as what was lacking from it."
"27604","(27604) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whatever is broken of it, if it is not black, it will be reckoned. That"
"27605","(27605) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ali bin Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa’id bin splint; In a tooth, if some of it becomes black, then calculate its level as a fraction."
"27606","(27606) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: If half of it is broken, or a third, then White, so on account of what was broken of it."
"27607","(27607) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the case of a black tooth, if it is damaged, it will be governed by people of justice."
"27608","(27608) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In the black sunnah there is a government."
"27609","(27609) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: It contains a third of the blood money."
"27610","(27610) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It contains a third of her blood money."
"27611","(27611) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: It contains a third of the blood money."
"27612","(27612) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar; A black tooth includes a third of its time."
"27613","(27613) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraida On the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab, he said: If a black tooth is removed and is fixed, one-third This is what"
"27614","(27614) Hafs and Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Bukair bin Abdullah bin al-Ashaj, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; He decreed that one hundred dinars should be paid for the existing spring when it was extinguished."
"27615","(27615) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: It contains a third of the blood money."
"27616","(27616) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It contains a third of her blood money."
"27617","(27617) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt; Omar ibn Abdul Aziz made a judgment in the case of a standing spring that was estimated at one hundred dinars."
"27618","(27618) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Al-Sha’bi (h), on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; They said: In the existing spring there is the rule of just people."
"27619","(27619) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: In the existing spring, when it is harvested, a third of its blood money."
"27620","(27620) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq, who said: There is a ruling in the one-eyed eye."
"27621","(27621) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abdullah bin Buraidah, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Ya`mar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar; For the one-eyed eye, if it was cut short and it was standing: a third of its blood money."
"27622","(27622) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hakim, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib, who said: It was during the case when Abu Bakr and Omar made a case: that when a man spread it out, his owner did not take it. Or He seized it and did not spread it, or it was cut off from the earth and it did not reach it. And whatever it decreases, there will be a reckoning."
"27623","(27623) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali, who said: A man is entitled to half the blood money."
"27624","(27624) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: A man is entitled to half the blood money."
"27625","(27625) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, (H), on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In If the hand is injured and paralyzed, or the leg, or the eye, if its sight is lost and it is standing, then its sanity has been achieved."
"27626","(27626) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Omar, who said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: There are fifty per man."
"27627","(27627) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: A man has fifty camels in fifths."
"27628","(27628) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hamid bin Hilal, who said: In a book written by Marwan, on the authority of Zaid bin Thabit: If you cut a man’s hair, then half the blood money is due on her."
"27629","(27629) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim ibn Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In the jifayyah, a third The blood money"
"27630","(27630) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: In a dead animal is a third of the blood money."
"27631","(27631) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: In a dead animal is a third of the blood money. Fifths."
"27632","(27632) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In a dead animal is a third of the blood money."
"27633","(27633) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Makhoul, (h) and on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decreed a third of the blood money for the dead animal."
"27634","(27634) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The dead in the stomach and thigh, one-third of it is given. The blood money"
"27635","(27435) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Some people were throwing arrows, and one of them shot an arrow by mistake, and it hit a man in the stomach, so he pushed it back to his back. He was treated and recovered, then he was taken to Abu Bakr, who judged him with two bodies."
"27636","(27436) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid; In the window in the belly is a third of the blood money, and in the other is a hundred dinars."
"27637","(27637) Hatim bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhul, who said: The cavity is in the stomach until it emerges from the other side. Two hollows"
"27638","(27638) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who shot another man and he shot him up, saying: There are two dead bodies in it."
"27639","(27639) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said: In a dead animal is a third of the blood money."
"27640","(27440) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit, who said: In every window in A part of the hand and foot, one hundred dinars."
"27641","(27641) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A third of the blood money is given to a carcass in the thigh."
"27642","(27442) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, who said: Every penetrating organ is I paid her ransom a third of the blood money of that organ."
"27643","(27443) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: For every dry bone, every A hollow bone, so I made it hollow on account of that bone."
"27644","(27444) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abi Hisham, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr Ibn Hazm, he said: Omar said: Every throw that penetrates an organ, it contains a third of the blood money of that organ."
"27645","(27645) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Layla narrated to us, on the authority of Ikrimah bin Khalid, on the authority of a man from the family of Umar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Concerning the blood money. (Abdul Razzaq 17636)"
"27646","(27646) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: Concerning the blood money."
"27647","(27647) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The blood money is paid in fifths."
"27648","(27648) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: Concerning the blood money."
"27649","(27649) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said: Concerning the blood money."
"27650","(27650) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning the blood-moneyed male."
"27651","(27651) Abdul Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, decided the blood money for the male. (Abu Dawud 265)"
"27652","(27652) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: Was the penis removed? He said: Blood money. I said: What do you think if the scales are affected, and then something of what is left is affected? He said: wound."
"27653","(27653) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: In The blood-moneyed male"
"27654","(27454) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr made a ruling regarding a dhikr. A man with a hundred camels."
"27655","(27655) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled. In the case of a penis, if it is removed or its glans is cut off: the full blood of a hundred camels."
"27656","(27456) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah, who said: Concerning the glans if it is cut off. The blood money, so whatever is short of it will be accounted for."
"27657","(27657) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Zakaria, or Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, He said: In the bloodworm."
"27658","(27658) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Concerning the blood money."
"27659","(27659) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Salam, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Concerning the bloodworm."
"27660","(27660) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: In the blood vessel."
"27661","(27661) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: In The only part is the blood money."
"27662","(27662) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What do you think if the palanquin is affected? He said: Blood money. He said: I said to Ataa: Should I prove it? He said: They said that."
"27663","(27663) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, he said: Zuhair narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, He said: In the bloodworm."
"27664","(27644) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Masruq; There is a ruling on the hand if it is cut off, and there is a ruling on the molar, meaning something that is eaten."
"27665","(27665) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab, who said: In the hand If a third of the blood money is cut, then"
"27666","(27666) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: In the hand is splintering if it is cut. a third of the blood money"
"27667","(27667) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Urwah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, on the authority of Yahya bin Yamar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab; In the hand are the spoils if a third of the blood money is cut off."
"27668","(27668) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of Yahya ibn Umar, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In the hand are the spoils if a third of the blood money is cut off."
"27669","(27669) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the hand are the shackles. They said: There is a ruling by just people."
"27670","(27670) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: If the hand or leg is broken, then She was healed and nothing was missing from her: her bribes were one hundred and eighty dirhams."
"27671","(27671) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the hand, or the foot if it is broken, make peace."
"27672","(27672) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan; Omar gave a ruling regarding a man whose leg was broken and it was splinted and straightened, so he ruled on it for twenty dinars.\n He said: It was said to him: Indeed, she has become weak."
"27673","(27673) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sa’id bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh: Concerning a man who broke another man’s hand. So it was forced, and Shurayh said: On the breaker is the reward of the one who pulls back. But praise be to God that He restored His hand to him."
"27674","(27674) Waki’ told us, he said: Shu’abi told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Concerning all the members. Government"
"27675","(27675) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; Fifty dinars are to be broken on the leg, and if it is healed on 'Uthm, there are fifty dinars in it, and whatever is in it is given to the bone."
"27676","(27676) Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yassar, who said: In the forearm, And the leg, the humerus, and the thigh, if they are broken and then splinted: Qalusan, Qalusan."
"27677","(27677) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, I said to him: The hand was broken, or the leg, or The clavicle was forced and straightened. He said: There is something about that, but I have not heard of it."
"27678","(27678) Abu Dawud al-Tayalisi told us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of al-Hasan; Concerning a man whose hand was broken, he said: He will be compensated for his hand. He said: And Muhammad said: Shurayh said: He will be given the reward of a doctor."
"27679","(27679) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the one whose arm is broken, then he is redressed, he said: something will be reconciled to him."
"27680","(27680) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; He decreed that if the nail fell and did not grow, or grew with change: ten dinars, and if it came out white, then five dinars. dinars"
"27681","(27681) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha’, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In the case of a nail with one eye, one-fifth of the blood money for a finger."
"27682","(27682) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Siwar, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He made a judgment on the nail of a man who was injured by a one-eyed man, with ten diyahs for a finger."
"27683","(27683) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning the nail, if it grows, if there is a defect in it. A camel"
"27684","(27684) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib; Omar ibn al-Khattab made a ruling regarding the victory if he was arrogant and corrupted by a reduction."
"27685","(27685) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim; In the case of a fawn, if it does not grow, then there are two she-camels in it, but if it grows blind and has no white spot, then there is a she-camel in it."
"27686","(27686) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; If the nail does not grow, then it includes Bint Makhad, and if it does not grow, then it includes Bint Labun."
"27687","(27687) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ about the nail if it did not grow? He said: I heard something about it, but I don’t know what it is."
"27688","(27688) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me; The commanders of the army and the people of opinion gathered to support Omar bin Abdul Aziz in defeating him, and if he was defeated, he would suffer, or fall, or be blackened: The tenth of the money of a finger is ten dinars."
"27689","(27689) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Amr ibn Haram, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; In the case of a nail with one eye, one-fifth of the blood money for a finger."
"27690","(27690) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded retaliation at the age of the age, and said: God’s Book is retaliation. (Bukhari 6894, Abu Dawud 4585)"
"27691","(27691) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Azhar, on the authority of Muharib bin Dathar, who said: Two men came to Shurayh. He broke this one's molar, and this one's tooth, he said: This is a bend in a tooth, stand up."
"27692","(27692) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hasan, who said: There is no retaliation for bones except for the tooth, or the head."
"27693","(27693) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He is led from the Sunnah."
"27694","(27694) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: What is the spring from? He said: Yes, and the Sunnah."
"27695","(27695) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Muslim bin Jundub, on the authority of Aslam Mawla Omar, he said: I heard Omar on the pulpit saying: In the rib is a camel."
"27696","(27696) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the rib, if it is broken by a camel, then if it is forced by a camel."
"27697","(27697) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Asim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; There is a camel in the rib."
"27698","(27698) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’ba, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Shu’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, and Masruq; They said: In the rib and the like, if it is broken and put on something other than a bone, they said: It is the reward of a doctor."
"27699","(27699) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Salim, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit, who said: There are ten dinars"
"27700","(27700) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, on the authority of al-Hakam, he said: In the rib is a camel, and in the molar A camel"
"27701","(27701) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim bin Damra, on the authority of Ali, who said: In one The two eggs are half the blood money."
"27702","(27702) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali; Like him"
"27703","(27703) Zayd ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd ibn Thabit (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ali (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah ibn Al-Zubayr (h) and on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Amr ibn Shuaib; They said: The two eggs are equal."
"27704","(27704) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: In The blood money is full, fifty-fifty."
"27705","(27705) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid; The two eggs are the same, fifty by fifty, and I did not hear it for certain."
"27706","(27706) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: The two eggs? He said: Fifty-fifty, but I did not hear it from proven sources."
"27707","(27707) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The two eggs are equal."
"27708","(27708) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Shu’bi, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Both females are equal."
"27709","(27709) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: In Al-Bayda Al-Yusra Two-thirds of the blood money, and a third in the right hand. I said: Why? He said: Because if the left one is gone, no children will be born to him, and if the right hand is gone, he will have no children."
"27710","(27710) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I mentioned that to Ibrahim, and he said: They are all the same."
"27711","(27711) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Masruq, he said: There is a ruling on the tongue of the mute."
"27712","(27712) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the tongue of the mute is the complete blood money."
"27713","(27713) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; There is a ruling on the tongue of a mute, and there is a ruling on the remembrance of a eunuch."
"27714","(27714) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of his followers, who said: In the tongue of a mute person is a third of what is in the tongue of a sound person."
"27715","(27715) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: In the tongue of a mute is the complete blood sacrifice."
"27716","(27716) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: In mentioning the one who does not have intercourse with women, such as What is in the male who has intercourse with women? He said: Yes, and he said to me: Have you seen the one from whom that was gone? Will he not fulfill his vow?"
"27717","(27717) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Abdul Aziz bin Omar informed me; The commanders of the soldiers and the people of opinion among them gathered to treat Omar bin Abdulaziz in the case of the sinful if it was broken, then repair it. Other than 'Uthm, it contains forty dinars."
"27718","(27718) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: He informed me on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; If the sin is broken, forty dinars."
"27719","(27719) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Azhar al-Attar, on the authority of Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: In hernia, one-third of the blood money."
"27720","(27720) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: In the bladder hernia, one-third The blood money"
"27721","(27721) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: He informed me on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, he said: Concerning the bladder when it is pierced, A third of the blood money was not retained by urine."
"27722","(27722) Abu Asama told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid; In hernia, blood money."
"27723","(27723) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ruled on the crucifixion. The blood money (Abu Dawud 263. Bayhaqi 95)"
"27724","(27724) Abu Khaled and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zaid, who said: In the blood of blood."
"27725","(27725) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Concerning the blood is blood money."
"27726","(27726) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The people of knowledge are agreed that there is blood in the steel."
"27727","(27727) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muslim, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, he said: In the crucifixion is blood money."
"27728","(27728) Muhammad bin Bakr narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, who said: Abu Bakr judged the man’s crucifixion. If it is broken, then he is repared with the full blood money, if it is not borne by him, and with half the blood money if it is borne by him."
"27729","(27729) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Ibn Abi Najih told me, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If he is injured The crucifixion, or it was broken and repaired and his semen was cut off, then the blood money is sufficient, but if the semen was not cut off and it was apparent Incline, it is seen in it."
"27730","(27730) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I asked Ata’ about steel being broken? He said: Blood money."
"27731","(27731) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Muhammad bin Al-Harith bin Sufyan informed me; That Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abi Rabi’a told him; He said: I was with Ibn al-Zubayr about a man whose backbone was broken, and he stooped and did not sit while he walked. He was hunched over, so he said: Walk, so he walked, and two-thirds of the blood money was paid for him."
"27732","(27732) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Yazid the Huge, on the authority of Ali, He said: If the penis is broken and intercourse is prevented, then the blood money is required."
"27733","(27733) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Zayd bin Thabit; He paid a quarter of her blood money for a woman’s breastfeeding, and an eighth of her blood money for a man’s breastfeeding."
"27734","(27734) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: In the breasts, the blood money."
"27735","(27735) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: In the woman’s breast and above is the blood money. In full, and in one of them is half the blood money."
"27736","(27736) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: In the two breasts is the blood money, and in one of them is half. The blood money"
"27737","(27737) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: He was asked about a woman’s breasts? He said: It is half the blood money, and if some of it is lost, then it is the judgment of diligent justice."
"27738","(27738) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Amr bin Shuaib said: Abu Bakr made a ruling regarding a man’s breast. If his nipple is removed by five camels, and he performs the ejaculation of a woman’s breast by ten camels if only the nipple of her breast is affected, If it is cut from its roots, then fifteen camels."
"27739","(27739) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: Muammar told me, on the authority of someone who told him, on the authority of Ikrimah; Abu Bakr made a hundred dinars for the nipple of a woman’s breast, and he made fifty dinars for the nipple of a man’s breast."
"27740","(27740) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Dawud bin Abi Asim informed me; That Abd al-Malik ibn Marwan made a ruling for fifty dinars in the fight against Ghassan, and they wounded the women in the breast."
"27741","(27741) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, he said: He informed me on the authority of Abraham, he said: In a woman’s breast is half the blood money. And in the breast of a man is a ruler."
"27742","(27742) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: A woman’s breast is half of her brain, even if She was barren."
"27743","(27743) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn al-Harithi, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He did not reap The servant: for his own slave, and he gives his master a choice: if he wishes, he may ransom him, and if he wishes, he may pay him back."
"27744","(27744) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: The slave’s crime is on his neck. He gives his master a choice: if he wishes, he may ransom him, and if he wishes, he may pay him back."
"27745","(27745) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: A slave does not earn from his master more than one price. My neck"
"27746","(27746) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Whatever the servant commits is on his own neck, Or his master will take care of him."
"27747","(27747) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, he said: I told him: A slave committed a crime. He said: On his neck."
"27748","(27748) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed on the authority of Salim bin Abdullah, he said: If people wish The slaves may be redeemed with the help of the wounds of the wounded, and if they wish, they may surrender to them."
"27749","(27749) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: If he kills by mistake: If his master wishes, he may ransom him, and if he wishes, he can pay him back. Completely"
"27750","(27750) Suleiman bin Harb told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Zaid, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; He used to say about a servant who commits a crime. He said: He is his master with the option. If He wishes, He may repel the slave with the crime, and if He wishes, He may grant the crime and keep the slave."
"27751","(27751) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he committed a crime, he learned of his crime, then he set him free; He is a guarantor of his crime."
"27752","(27752) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, the same."
"27753","(27753) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a slave who drags a puppy and his master frees him. It is permissible to free him, and his master guarantees his price."
"27754","(27754) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad; Concerning a slave who commits a crime. He said: Concerning his neck. I said: What if his master frees him? He said: It is worth it."
"27755","(27755) Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a servant who committed a crime, and his master found out about it and freed him. He said: The servant is striving for his crime."
"27756","(27756) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir bin Hazim, on the authority of Hammad; He was asked about a servant who commits a crime? He said: His master has the option. If he wishes, he can pay him, and if he wishes, he can surrender him. If he frees him, then he pays the price of a slave, not the slave’s obligation. Something if he is freed."
"27757","(27757) Waki’ told us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khalid, peace be upon him, told us: Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a slave who killed a free man, then his master informed him and he freed him. He said: His emancipation is permissible, and his master must pay the blood money."
"27758","(27758) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: If his master freed him and he knew of the crime, then He is a guarantor against the crime, and if he did not know about the crime, then he is responsible for the value of the slave."
"27759","(27759) Hatim bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a freed slave kills, he will be given to him. The guardians of the murdered person. If they wished, they could kill him, and if they wished, they could keep him alive."
"27760","(27760) Muhammad ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I do not know that blood is given except to its family members. If they wish, they can sell it. And if they wish, they will be rewarded, and if they will, they will be guided."
"27761","(27761) Hatem bin Wardan told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a slave who was killed as a free man and his heirs were given the right to kill him. He said: If he wishes, they can enslave him."
"27762","(27762) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It should be paid to the guardians of the murdered person. They kill if they want, and if they want, they enslave."
"27763","(27763) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer (h) and on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; They said: If they wished, they could be killed, and if they wished, they could be enslaved."
"27764","(27764) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salem, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; Concerning a slave who was killed intentionally as a free man. He said: These will be given: the family of the killed person. If they wish, they can kill him, and if they wish, they can enslave him."
"27765","(27765) Abbad told us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a slave who intentionally kills a free man, he said: It is not theirs to use him, but theirs is his blood. If they wish, they can kill him, and if If they wish, they will pardon him."
"27766","(27766) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a slave who kills a free man intentionally, and then the guardian of blood pardons the blood, he said: He returns to his master."
"27767","(27767) Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If they pardon him, the slave will return to his master."
"27768","(27768) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a slave who was killed as a free man and was handed over to his guardians, he said: If they pardon him, he will return to his master, and they have no right to They use it.\n Waki` said: This is the saying of Sufyan."
"27769","(27769) Hafs, Ali, and Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin al-Musayyab He said: Its value is as high as it has been."
"27770","(27770) Ismail bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Amr bin Muhajir, and Sawad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz. He said: Its value on the day it is afflicted."
"27771","(27771) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Omar, on the authority of Ayyub bin Musa, on the authority of Ata’ and Makhul, and Ibn Shihab, they said: Its value on the day it is afflicted."
"27772","(27772) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin, that they said: Its value on the day it is afflicted is a certain amount. She reached it."
"27773","(27773) Muammar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Its value is on the day it is afflicted."
"27774","(27774) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan, they said: : Its value on the day it is struck, as high as it has been."
"27775","(27775) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ali, Abdullah and Shuraih, They said: Its price, and if the money is returned, it is free."
"27776","(27776) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: It is wealth that has not reached its value."
"27777","(27777) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He conveys what he conveyed."
"27778","(27778) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Sha’bi; Sa`id ibn al-Aas made the blood money of a slave who was killed by mistake four thousand, and his price was more than that, and he said: I hate to He made his blood money greater than the blood money of a free man."
"27779","(27779) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The blood money of a free man will not be reached by him."
"27780","(27780) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The master does not add anything to the blood money of a free man. (Abdul Razzaq 18169)"
"27781","(27781) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, and al-Shu’bi, who said: He will not reach his beginning. The slave is the free man in error."
"27782","(27782) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The blood money of a slave is less than his blood money. The free one"
"27783","(27783) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the servant’s ear or eye is afflicted, then it is in it. Half of its price, and if its ears or eyes are damaged, then its full price is paid, and it should be paid to the one who injured it."
"27784","(27784) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If the slave’s eye is gouged out, or cut out His hand, or his foot; He pays half his value, and if his eyes are gouged out, or his hands or legs are cut off, he pays it and pays his value."
"27785","(27785) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the case of a property, if its kind is lost, then half of its price is paid."
"27786","(27786) Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salama, on the authority of Iyas bin Muawiyah; Concerning a man who intentionally cut off the hand of a servant, or gouged out his eye, he said: It is his, and his price is due."
"27787","(27787) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, in a free man a slave is injured. He said: If he puts out his eye, then it is in it. Half its price"
"27788","(27788) Wakī’ told us, on the authority of Al-Nāḥas ibn Qaym, on the authority of Ata’; In Mudhahit Al-Abd, half an eighth of an eighth."
"27789","(27789) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakaria, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; In Mudhahit Al-Abd, half an eighth of an eighth."
"27790","(27790) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He ruled on the age of the slave and his explanation was based on Estimate its value from its price; Half a tenth of its value, like the blood money of al-Hurr fi al-Sunnah and al-Muddahiyah."
"27791","(27791) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh; In the same way"
"27792","(27792) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A slave’s wounds are from his price. Like the surgeon of a free man who died, ten and a half tenths."
"27793","(27793) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The servant’s mind is worth its price."
"27794","(27794) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The servant’s wounds were in Its price is like the wounds of a freed man, and Al-Zuhri said: Some people said: It is only money, so it is based on what is deducted from its price."
"27795","(27795) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salamah, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: Surgeries are performed Slaves are subject to the same wounds as freedmen."
"27796","(27796) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abu Hurri, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a free man who took something from a slave, he said: He shall return to his master what he had diminished in his price."
"27797","(27797) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The mind of a servant is worth its price. Like the mind of a free man in his life."
"27798","(27798) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Husayn al-Harithi, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, said: The wounds of slaves are performed in the same way as the wounds of free people are performed."
"27799","(27799) Hushaym and Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih; Concerning a slave who wounded a free man, he said: If he wishes, he can take retaliation from him, and if he wishes, he can take hundreds of pounds with his fist."
"27800","(27800) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a free man intentionally cuts a slave, it is only a blood money. He has no power over him."
"27801","(27801) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: A free man cannot be led by a slave."
"27802","(27802) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hasan (h) and Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no retaliation between the owned and the free for what is less than one's life."
"27803","(27803) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: The slave punctures the free man, or gouges out his eye. So the free person wants to take advantage of the slave. He said: A free person does not take advantage of the slave. Mujahid and Suleiman said something like that. Bin Musa"
"27804","(27804) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed on the authority of Salim, he said: A slave does not take the liberty of a free man."
"27805","(27805) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no force between a free man and a slave, except If a slave kills a free man, he will be killed for it."
"27806","(27806) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam and Hammad, who said: There is no retaliation among the kings."
"27807","(27807) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi, on the authority of al-Hasan (h), on the authority of al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, They said: There is no retaliation among the slaves for what is less than one's life."
"27808","(27808) Abbad told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Shu’abi; They said: There is no retaliation between the kings, and there is no retaliation between the children."
"27809","(27809) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: I was informed on the authority of Salem, that he said: If a Mamluk baptizes and is killed If a slave is killed, or if he hurts him, then he is a victim of retaliation."
"27810","(27810) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Aziz, who said: The slaves are led by The property in every pillar reaches its value itself, so anything less than that is considered as landfill."
"27811","(27811) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Omar; That in a book by Omar bin Abdul Aziz, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab: The slaves are led by the slaves for an intentional period of up to Himself and what is less than that."
"27812","(27812) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, And Al-Sha’abi, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud, said: A servant is not led by another servant for his wounds intentionally, or by mistake, except in Premeditated murder"
"27813","(27813) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to see retribution among the slaves."
"27814","(27814) Shababi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: He said: I saw Nawfal ibn Musahaq taking retribution for slaves. Some of them from each other."
"27815","(27815) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He saw no harm in A man is killed by two men, such that one of them is killed, and the blood money is taken from the other."
"27816","(27816) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning a man killed by a group, he said: They will be given to the friends of the killed person, and they will kill whomever they wish, and pardon whomever they wish."
"27817","(27817) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he pardons one of them, let him pardon them. All of you"
"27818","(27818) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Hisham?? , on the authority of Al-Hassan; He said about a man who was killed by three people, and his guardian wanted to pardon some, kill others, and take from others. The blood money, he said: He does not have that."
"27819","(27819) Baz bin Asad told us, on the authority of Aban Al-Attar, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Concerning a man who is killed by a group, he said: He pardons whomever he wants, kills whomever he wants, and takes blood money from whomever he wants."
"27820","(27820) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who is killed by a group, he said: He kills whomever he wants, pardons whomever he wants, and takes blood money from whomever he wants."
"27821","(27821) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, He said: The fetus of a mother is ten dinars."
"27822","(27822) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Khaliq, on the authority of Hammad, who said: There is a ruling in the fetus of a mother."
"27823","(27823) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The fetus of a mother, when it begins, its value is one day. He began"
"27824","(27824) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: They used to take the fetus of the mothers from the fetus. The heat"
"27825","(27825) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: In the fetus of a mother from her price, similar to the fetus of a free woman from her blood money. A tenth, and a half-tenth."
"27826","(27826) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, who said: If he falls alive, then he pays his price, and if He died, so he owes one-tenth of the eighth of his mother."
"27827","(27827) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the mother’s fetus is one-tenth of its eighth."
"27828","(27828) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: One tenth of its eighth."
"27829","(27829) Abu Bakr told us, he said: I heard a man saying: Sufyan said: And we say: If it is a boy, then half a tenth. Its value, and if she is a slave girl, then one tenth of its value if she were alive."
"27830","(27830) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the garden of the animal its value."
"27831","(27831) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: They used to take the fetus of the animal from the The mother's fetus"
"27832","(27832) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the foetus of the animal is a tenth of the eighth of its mother."
"27833","(27833) Omar told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning the animal embryo, he said: We see the animal as a commodity, and its embryo is judged by the judge, what he sees in his opinion."
"27834","(27834) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Israel narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; In the offspring of beasts there is a government."
"27835","(27835) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made a ruling regarding the fetus; A slave, or a mother, and he said: The one who judged it: Is he of sound mind who neither drinks, nor eats, nor shouts? So he made it permissible, and the like of that. Does it appear? Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: This is to say the words of a poet, in which a male or female slave was deceived. (Abu Dawud 4568, Tirmidhi 1410)"
"27836","(27836) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Miswar ibn Makhramah, who said: Omar consulted Ibn al-Khattab, regarding the woman’s death, and he said: Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bab: I witnessed the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decree it. With deceit; A male or female slave, he said: Then Omar said to him: Bring someone who testified with you, and Muhammad bin Muslim testified for him.\n(Bukhari 6907, Abu Dawud 4559)"
"27837","(27837) Abu Osama told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: In The fetus is a stranger; A slave, a female slave, or a mule. (Abu Dawud 4568)"
"27838","(27838) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: There is a male slave, or a female slave, or a mare in it."
"27839","(27839) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Ghura; A slave, or a slave to his mother, or to the people closest to him."
"27840","(27840) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, and Al-Hakam; They said: The fetus of a free woman is a slave or a female slave."
"27841","(27841) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man who struck his wife’s stomach and she had a miscarriage. He said: He is tempted and he inherits from her and she inherits from him."
"27842","(27842) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, and Mujahid; They said: In the desert there is a slave, or a female slave, or a horse."
"27843","(27843) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: A slave, or a female slave, or a horse."
"27844","(27844) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Concerning a woman who drank medicine. So she miscarried. He said: You will free his slaves and give his father a slave."
"27845","(27845) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abdul-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He said: A slave or a female slave. (Musnad 1901)"
"27846",""
"27847","(27847) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h) and Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; They said about whoever afflicts a fetus: He is obligated to free a slave along with the slaves."
"27848","(27848) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of the ruling, he said: I heard him say: If a woman is struck and she miscarries His companion will be freed."
"27849","(27849) Ibn Uyaynah and Waki` narrated to us, saying: Omar bin Dhar narrated to us, on the authority of Mujahid; A woman wiped another woman’s stomach and she had a miscarriage, so Omar bin Al-Khattab ordered her to be freed."
"27850","(27850) Waki’ narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: The amount of money is five hundred percent."
"27851","(27851) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, who said: The value of the ghari is four hundred dirhams."
"27852","(27852) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam; Omar bin Al-Khattab valued the money at fifty dinars."
"27853","(27853) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed jealousy on the wise woman."
"27854","(27854) Yahya bin Saeed and Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Jealousy is upon the wise woman."
"27855","(27855) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ibn Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: In his wealth."
"27856","(27856) Yunus bin Muhammad narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Jabir; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, placed in the fetus a burden on the killer’s mind, and healed her husband and two children.\n(Bukhari 67400 Muslim 1309)"
"27857","(27857) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ubaid bin Nudhaylah, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, decided to pay the blood money for her living relatives, and for the pregnancy, Ghura.\n(Muslim 1310, Abu Dawud 4557)"
"27858","(27858) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Abdullah bin Qusayt, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab ; Omar made the Ghurā on the people of the village, and the obligations on the people of the desert."
"27859","(27859) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: The blood money for the fetus is on the one who He has done well in his property, and there is nothing wrong with his people."
"27860","(27860) Ismail bin Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, on the authority of Ali; He said: There is no retaliation for a dead person, nor a person being led in prayer, nor a person being transported."
"27861","(27861) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no fuel in the dead, the dead, and the dead. The blood money was only taken from the man’s wealth."
"27862","(27862) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He is not led from a dead animal, nor from a dead person. The one who is being led in prayer, nor of the one who is transported, nor of anything in which there is fear for the soul, nor of anything that does not come as happened. His companion"
"27863","(27863) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah bin Ubaid Al-Kala’i, on the authority of an alcoholic, who said: He should not be led away from Al-Jāifīfah, Al-Ma’amumah, Al-Munqilah, and Al-Nakhira."
"27864","(27864) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of al-Zuhri, who said: It is not in the case of a mother, nor in a dead body, nor in the case of a dead person. Broken bones are retaliation."
"27865","(27865) Abu Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of Issa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no retaliation in a prisoner, nor a person being led in prayer, nor a person who transports him. Nor in the thigh if it is broken."
"27866","(27866) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, who said: I saw Ibn al-Zubayr leading one of his people in congregation. He said: I saw them walking together in trust."
"27867","(27867) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed; That Ibn al-Zubayr drove from his mount."
"27868","(27868) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar; Ibn al-Zubayr quoted from his narration, saying: So the people were amazed, or he made the people marvel."
"27869","(27869) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Omar, who said: We are not bound by bones."
"27870","(27870) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ibn Abi Malika, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: There is no retaliation in the bones."
"27871","(27871) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, who said: Omar bin Abdulaziz wrote: If there is a broken bone, there is no retaliation. Therein"
"27872","(27872) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir; They said: There is no retaliation for a bone."
"27873","(27873) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: It is not in any of the bones?? Retaliation, except for the face and head."
"27874","(27874) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: There is no retaliation for breaking bones."
"27875","(27875) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi and Al-Hasan, who said: There is no retaliation in the bones."
"27876","(27876) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the hand and leg are broken, it is not There is retaliation for the one who breaks it, but the blood money is upon him."
"27877","(27877) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali; He was responsible for the commander, the driver, and the passenger."
"27878","(27878) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Husayn, on the authority of Shuraih (H) and on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, (H) On the authority of Tariq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, they said: He includes the commander, the driver, and the passenger."
"27879","(27879) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I heard him say: If a man drives his animal If he drives her gently, he is not liable, but if he is violent in his drive and she is injured, then he is liable."
"27880","(27880) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The driver and the commander are guaranteed."
"27881","(27881) Abbad narrated to us, on the authority of Omar bin Amir, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Khallas, on the authority of Ali, who said: If the road is wide, then Guarantee on it."
"27882","(27882) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The commander is fined. I said: The driver is fined by the hand. And the man? He said: They claimed that he was in love with the hand, so I repeated him, and he said: He says: The way is the way."
"27883","(27883) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Al-Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: The driver and the commander, The rider will be fined if his animal hits, steps on, or hits a hand or a leg."
"27884","(27884) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos, who said: He guarantees the leader and the driver. And the passenger did not hit the front."
"27885","(27885) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Khalas, on the authority of Ali, who said: He includes the radifan."
"27886","(27886) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: There is no warranty on the buttocks."
"27887","(27887) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; Concerning the backbone, he said: They are partners."
"27888","(27888) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The rider and the buttocks are equal, as long as they are lowered, so it is There are two halves between them."
"27889","(27889) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, and Abu Hashim, who said: The spanking guarantees what guarantees Introduction"
"27890","(27890) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He guarantees the buttocks."
"27891","(27891) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Reason is upon the people of the Diwan."
"27892","(27892) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Hurr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Reason is upon the people of the Diwan."
"27893","(27893) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: Omar was the first to make the blood money ten. A tenth in the gifts of the fighters, not the people."
"27894","(27894) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Ibn Muhammad bin Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Salouli, on the authority of Muadh bin Jabal, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah, who said: The crime of the one who plots against his master."
"27895","(27895) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The crime of the one who plots against his master."
"27896","(27896) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, who said: Yasir al-Mukhtib narrated to me, that a woman arranged for a female slave She committed a crime, so Omar bin Abdul Aziz ruled that her crimes were committed against her mistress in the value of the maidservant."
"27897","(27897) Ibn Aliya told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the criminality of the mastermind, he said: He is a slave. If his master wishes, he can surrender to him, and if he wishes, he may ransom him."
"27898","(27898) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If the plotter kills a person, or So he gouged out an item, and it was said to his master: Pay it back, or ransom it."
"27899","(27899) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Salim, on the authority of Amir, who said: The crime of the mastermind and the mother of the child is Ali. Her master is wise."
"27900","(27900) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Hammad, who said: The blood money is due on their companions if they are killed, and if they are killed, then I pay their ransom. The money of the owned."
"27901","(27901) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The crime of the one who plots it On her master"
"27902","(27902) Wakī’ narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan say: The crime committed against his master guarantees his value. Ibn Abi Layla said in Al-Mudabbar: He is liable for all crimes."
"27903","(27903) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The crime of a person being punished is on his neck, he begins with it."
"27904","(27904) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He will strive in it and in the one who is rewarded with quotas."
"27905","(27905) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The crime of writing is on one’s neck."
"27906","(27906) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The crime of writing to Ali Her master"
"27907","(27907) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of his companions, or on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever the decree attains is in it. His neck, he will perform his crime and write to all of him."
"27908","(27908) Waki’ told us, I heard Sufyan say: The crime of writing is on one’s neck."
"27909","(27909) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Whatever he collects in the decrees is for him. He uses it when writing it. This is what those before you used to say."
"27910","(27910) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever is committed in the decrees, it is for him."
"27911","(27911) Waki` narrated to us, saying: I heard Sufyan saying: If someone commits a crime against him, he will be his, not his master."
"27912","(27912) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa told us, on the authority of Sufyan bin Hussein, on the authority of Al-Hikam; He used to say regarding the crime committed against the child’s mother: It should not exceed her value. Hammad said: This is what it has committed."
"27913","(27913) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The crime of the child’s mother against Her master"
"27914","(27914) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; If the child’s mother commits a crime, then her master is responsible for her crimes."
"27915","(27915) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning the child’s mother, she is a jinn. He said: She rises up against her master."
"27916","(27916) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Zakaria, who said: Amer was asked about a concubine who killed a woman, and her master was not alive. He freed her, and she gave birth to him? He said: This is my mother. If his master wishes, he can take care of her, and if he wishes, he can surrender her entirely to her."
"27917","(27917) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhul, on the authority of Zaid, who said: In the mind is the blood."
"27918","(27918) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Concerning the mortal mind."
"27919","(27919) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Al-Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who frightened another man and caused him to lose his mind. He said: If Omar had caught him, he would have been responsible for him."
"27920","(27920) Suleiman bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Awf, he said: I heard a sheikh, before Ibn Al-Ash’ath’s tribulation, so I cursed him. They said: This is Abu Al-Muhallab, the uncle of Abu Qalabab. He said: A man threw a stone at his head, and his hearing, his tongue, and his mind were gone. And he remembered him, but he did not approach women, so he decided for a lifetime to pay four blood money."
"27921",""
"27922","(27922) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whoever builds anything other than his heaven is liable."
"27923","(27923) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Shuraih, who said: He used to guarantee the owners of the places that You take it on the road, and the bulls of mules, and the wood that is put in the walls, and he did not include the external wells. The ones in front of the coffin in the cemetery, and the ones in the graves, and what has been made for the benefit of Muslims."
"27924","(27924) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus, who said: Whoever sets up a peg in a land other than his own, and his heavens are not within It is correct, and whoever digs a well in a place other than its land or sky, is liable for what falls into it."
"27925","(27925) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: Whoever removes anything from his house to On the way, something happened, so he is responsible for it. Whoever digs a stone, stick, or digs a well on the path of Muslims, his blood money will be taken, but he will not be led away from it."
"27926","(27926) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Whoever innovates anything in the way of Muslims, He is a guarantor."
"27927","(27927) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who narrated it, saying: Whoever removes something from his limit and hits something, then he Guarantor (Bazzar 3664)"
"27928","(27928) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: When a man begins the prayer Or the wood in its wall within it."
"27929","(27929) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Mis`ar narrated to us, on the authority of Wasil al-Ahdab al-Asadi, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, on the authority of Ali; He used to cut the cloth, or order it to be cut."
"27930","(27930) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Shuraih; He used to guarantee the barricade of Al-Suqiyyi and its pillar, and he said: He took it out in a place other than his kingdom."
"27931","(27931) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; Amr bin Al-Harith bin Al-Mustaliq dug a well on the path of the Muslims, and a mule fell into it and broke, so a piece of water secured it."
"27932","(27932) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Issa bin Dinar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, that Amr bin Al-Harith dug a well on the road to Muslims, then a mule passed by, fell into it, and broke; So he guaranteed him a share of the value of the mule, two hundred dirhams, and gave him the mule."
"27933","(27933) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan Abi Musafir; A neighbor’s knives fell on a boy and killed him or injured him, so Shurayh said: If I had brought him, I would have guaranteed him."
"27934","(27934) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Shuraih; He did not leave his shadow so that a knight could not pass through it with his spear, and he would say: You built on the knight’s spear."
"27935","(27935) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They were fined for intercourse, but they were not fined. From the breath"
"27936","(27936) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The owner of an animal is not liable for The breath"
"27937","(27937) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Shuraih; He was healed of the breath."
"27938","(27938) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Huzayl, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Peace and blessings of God be upon him: The man is a mighty one, which means a wretched one. (Abdul Razzaq 18376. Darqutni 213)"
"27939","(27939) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: The owner of the animal is responsible for what the animal harms. With her hand, or her feet, until he descends from her."
"27940","(27940) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man standing on his animal, and it struck. With her feet? Hammad said: He does not guarantee, and Al-Hakam said: He does."
"27941","(27941) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They were not guaranteed by the man. Unless he returns the rein."
"27942","(27942) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: If an animal strikes or brakes it, you are liable."
"27943","(27943) Sufyan bin Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Salama, and Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Abu Here, the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was informed of it. He said: The blind people’s wounds are mighty, the well is mighty, and the mine is Mighty, and in the five pillars. (Bukhari 1499, Muslim 6912)"
"27944","(27944) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ziyad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, like him, except that he did not mention her wound. (Bukhari 6913 and Muslim 1335)"
"27945","(27945) Waki’ told us, he said: Ibn Aoun told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The animals Its mind is mighty, and the mineral is its mighty mind, and the well is its mighty mind, and in the five pillars. (Ahmed 228, Tahawi 204)"
"27946","(27946) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Mughirah bin Abi Al-Hurr narrated to us; A camel preyed on a man and killed him, then a man came and killed the camel, so the man’s blood money was invalidated, and the man guaranteed the price of the camel."
"27947","(27947) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; A camel preyed on a man and killed him, then a man came and killed the camel, so Sharih voided the man’s blood money, and the man guaranteed its value. The camel"
"27948","(27948) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The one who kills animals will be fined, but their families will not be fined. What she killed?"
"27949","(27949) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Kill the stallion if it runs wild. upon you, and there will be no fine on you."
"27950","(27950) Muhammad bin Maysar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Abdul Karim; A stallion attacked a man and killed him, so he was brought to Abu Bakr and he fined it, and said: An animal that cannot be fathomed."
"27951","(27951) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad bin Qays, on the authority of Al-Hayy; A boy from his people entered upon Najiba of Zaid bin Suhan in his house, and she struck him and killed him, so his father came. With the sword, he made her barren. This was reported to Omar, so he shed the boy’s blood, and he guaranteed his father the price of the Najiba."
"27952","(27952) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who meets animals and fears that they will harm himself. He said: He will kill them and pay the price for them."
"27953","(27953) Ibn Numayr and Ya’la Ibn Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; If a man attacks a stallion and strikes it with a sword, is he liable? He said: Yes, except that Ibn Numayr said: He is guaranteed."
"27954","(27954) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was asked about the dowry that follows his mother? He said: He is a guarantor, because He sent you."
"27955","(27955) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning the dowry, he follows his mother. He said: He is guaranteed."
"27956","(27956) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad; I asked them about a dowry that follows its mother and is rewarded? They said: He guarantees."
"27957","(27957) Al-Bakrawi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He is not liable."
"27958","(27958) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Nafi’, who said: Omar said: Whatever befalls the one who escapes, there is no liability for his owner. Whoever harms the escaped person is liable."
"27959","(27959) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; Are you correct in the animal sent? They said: There is no warranty on him."
"27960","(27960) Abu Khaled told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Every messenger is guaranteed by its owner."
"27961","(27961) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man whose animal escaped while he was in his tracks, and hit a man. He said: There is nothing wrong with him, and the ruling said, for example: That"
"27962","(27962) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abu al-Muhallab, on the authority of Omar, he said: In The animal's eye is a quarter of its eighth."
"27963","(27963) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A quarter of its eighth is in the spring of a snake."
"27964","(27964) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Omar paid a quarter of its price for the animal’s eye."
"27965","(27965) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: Hisham bin Hubira Qadi wrote Al-Basra went to Shurayh and asked him about the creature’s eye? So he wrote to her: In the eye of the animal is a quarter of its price."
"27966","(27966) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ismail bin Abi Khaled narrated to us, on the authority of a man called: Habib, on the authority of Shuraih; He said: In the animal's eye is a quarter of its eighth."
"27967","(27967) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, or on the authority of Yazid bin Al-Walid, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who gouges out the eye of a one-eyed animal. He said: He pays its value to a one-eyed animal, and takes the animal."
"27968","(27968) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Shurayh; He said: Urwah Al-Baariqi came to me from Omar: In the eye of the animal is a quarter of its price."
"27969","(27969) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Shurayh, who said: With regard to the tail of the animal, if a quarter of Its price"
"27970","(27970) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He was asked about an animal whose tail or ears were cut off? He said: What is missing from her? If her hand or leg is cut off, then the value is the same."
"27971","(27971) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; Concerning a man who cut off the tail of an animal and said: “On him, its price,” and the animal will be paid to him."
"27972","(27972) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: Ali said: Whoever uses the property of a small people, or Great, so He is a guarantor."
"27973","(27973) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, on the authority of Ali, who said: Whoever seeks help from a young, free man or slave, and is distressed, then he A guarantor, and whoever seeks great help is not guarantored."
"27974","(27974) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If you seek the help of a mamluk People, you are responsible for what befalls you."
"27975","(27975) Saul bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who commands a child to do something without the permission of his family, then the child is destroyed. He said: He has a guarantee. If If he consulted with his family, there is no guarantee on him, and the same applies to a slave."
"27976","(27976) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I heard him say: If a man is burdened with His animal is a boy who has not yet reached puberty, and he harms something, then it is upon the one who carried it, but if he has reached puberty and harms something, then it is A guarantor, and there is a servant like that."
"27977","(27977) Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he hired him without their permission and he died, he would be fined."
"27978","(27978) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: The woman is divorced from her by her kinsfolk, and her sons inherit from her."
"27979","(27979) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, I heard him say: The child of a woman, the male, has more right With the inheritance of her master from her clan, even if it was a crime against her clan."
"27980","(27980) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Saleh, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Shurayh; Concerning a woman who freed a man, then she died. He said: Loyalty is to her children and discretion is upon them. He said: Amer used to say: Loyalty is to her children, and wisdom is upon them."
"27981","(27981) Muhammad bin Bakr Al-Barasani told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It is permissible for a woman to be blindfolded. And if she has a male child."
"27982","(27982) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not possible to recover from an intentional wound. Retaliation, it is the one who wronged his wealth rather than his mind."
"27983","(27983) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked the ruling about intentionality that cannot be taken from it? He said: Ali Al-Aqilah, and I asked Hammad? He said: In his wealth."
"27984","(27984) Muhammad bin Zaid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abi Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers, who said: Everything cannot be led from it, so it is Ali Al-Aqilah"
"27985","(27985) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, he said: Hisham told me, on the authority of his father, he said: Every intentional There is no money in it, then his mind is in the wealth of the one who is in need, and if he does not have money, then his money is in the money of the one who is in need, if he takes an oath. Intentionally, and the oath of the breaker had been broken before that, so her share is in the property of the breaker, so if he does not have any property then he must do so. His mind is like that, and if he had a left hand, he would not be able to do that. The mind is like that, and all the limbs are like that."
"27986","(27986) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Whatever killing occurs without a weapon, it is similar to that. Intentionally, the blood money is required by the wise one."
"27987","(27987) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Hammad about accidental, semi-intentional murder? He said: In the property of the killer, and the arbiter said: It is upon the wise man."
"27988","(27988) Abd al-Wahhab ibn Ata’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of al-Harith, and Ibn Shubramah, who said: He is upon you in What's wrong with him?"
"27989","(27989) Abd al-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his leaders, the same as him."
"27990","(27990) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: He was not struck by a whip, or A stone, or a stick, and it falls upon the soul, so it is like an intentional act, and it entails blood money, heavy for the rational person."
"27991","(27991) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: He was killed by the whip and the stick, like the pillars. Among them are a hundred camels, forty of them with their children in their bellies."
"27992","(27992) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The servant does not reason, nor can he be reasoned with."
"27993","(27993) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I told him: A man kills a slave, who Does he make sense? Is his mind, or his people? He said: His people."
"27994","(27994) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, and Al-Hakam; What they said about a man who killed an animal by mistake, they said: about his wealth, and if he kills a slave, then it is upon the sane person."
"27995","(27995) Omar told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a free man who killed a slave by mistake, he said: His value is on the sane person."
"27996","(27996) Waki’ told us, and Yazid bin Harun, on the authority of Zayd bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: If Al-Hurr kills The slave is a mistake, he frees a slave and owes the blood money."
"27997","(27997) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Rashid, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: The people of the tribe are not obligated to The servant's debt is one thing."
"27998","(27998) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A rational woman does not make peace, nor intentionally, nor a slave, nor In confession"
"27999","(27999) Ibn Idris narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A rational woman does not think of peace, nor intentionally, nor Confessingly, not as a slave."
"28000","(28000) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Hasan, and al-Sha’bi, who said: The fault lies with the wise, and with intention and righteousness. On the one who harmed him in his property."
"28001","(28001) Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He used to say: A rational woman does not reason with intention unless she wills, but the clan only reason with error."
"28002","(28002) Sharik told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, who said: The Muslims have agreed that a rational woman should not make peace, nor intentionally. And no confession."
"28003","(28003) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: The Sunnah has passed that the rational woman does not reason. This is intentionally done, except of one's own free will."
"28004","(28004) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Majid, who said: I fought a boy and cut off his nose. Then Abu Bakr brought me and examined me, but he did not find any retaliation, so he imposed blood money on my two maidens."
"28005","(28005) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: Concerning a child and an insane person, their sins and intentionality are equal to their sane minds."
"28006","(28006) Abbad told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Abraham, who said: The baptism of a boy and his sin is upon a wise woman."
"28007","(28007) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He baptized the boy. And his mistakes are the same."
"28008","(28008) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi (h) and al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, they said: The first The one who imposed the gift was Omar Ibn Al-Khattab, and he imposed the full blood money in three years, two-thirds of the blood money in two years, Half in two years, a third in one year, and less than that in one year."
"28009","(28009) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The blood money is within three years, the first In the year in which it is afflicted, two-thirds in two years, and a third in one year."
"28010","(28010) Muhammad bin Yazid told us, on the authority of Ayoub Abu Al-Ala, on the authority of his followers and Abu Hashim, who said: The blood money is in three days. Two years: two-thirds and a half in two years, and one-third in one year."
"28011","(28011) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The blood money is due over three years, for each one-third."
"28012","(28012) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ubaid, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It is not permissible to confess a boy, if she The clear proof of killing is upon him, so he is the wise one."
"28013","(28013) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Issa bin Abi Uzza, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; It was not permissible for a child and a slave to be together in resting places."
"28014","(28014) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Aban bin Salih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Masoud said: He used to say: The religion of the People of the Book is like the religion of a Muslim."
"28015","(28015) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Abdullah said: Whoever has a covenant or a covenant, the blood of a free Muslim will be ransomed.\n Sufyan said: Then Ali said after that: I do not know except that."
"28016","(28016) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Salih narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abdul Rahman On the authority of Abdullah, he said: Whoever has a covenant or a covenant, I will ransom him with the blood of a free Muslim."
"28017","(28017) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, he said: Such as the blood money of a Muslim."
"28018","(28018) Ismail bin Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid and Ata, who said: This is the promised period. Such as the blood money of a Muslim."
"28019","(28019) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of al-Sha’bi (h), on the authority of al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Diyah The Jew, the Christian, the Magian, and the covenant is like the blood money of a Muslim, and their wives are entitled to half of the men’s blood money. Amir was reciting these verses: {And if there is a people between you and them a covenant, then ransom is delivered to His family}"
"28020","(28020) Ismail bin Ibrahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard him say: This is the day of the covenants. The religion of the Muslim, and he recited these verses: {And if there be a people between you and them there is a covenant}"
"28021","(28021) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: The blood money of the people of the covenant is from The polytheists are like the religion of the Muslims."
"28022","(28022) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of My grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The blood money of an unbeliever is half that of a believer. (Abu Dawud 4573. Tirmidhi 1413)"
"28023","(28023) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dhakwan Abi Al-Zanad, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Al-Aziz, he said: The blood money of a covenant is half of the blood money of a Muslim."
"28024","(28024) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I read the book of Omar bin Abdul Aziz: The blood of the Jews The Christian is entitled to a third of the Muslim’s blood money."
"28025","(28025) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Al-Miqdam, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Khattab said: The blood money of a Jew and a Christian is four thousand, and the money of a Magi is eight hundred."
"28026","(28026) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Othman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah and Al-Hasan, who said: Diyah The blood money of a Jew and a Christian is four thousand, and the blood money of a Magi is eight hundred."
"28027","(28027) Yazid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Suleiman bin Yasar, he said: The people were In the first time they paid the money of the Magians with eight hundred percent, and they paid the money of the Jews and Christians with the same. They were dealing with it among themselves, then the blood money was returned to six thousand dirhams."
"28028","(28028) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The blood money of a Jew and a Christian is four thousand. The cost of the Magi is eight hundred."
"28029","(28029) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Nafi’, and Amr bin Dinar; They used to say: The blood money of a Jew and a Christian is four thousand."
"28030","(28030) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Sadiqah bin Yasar, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; Othman made a payment for the blood money of the Jew and the Christian of four thousand."
"28031","(28031) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Abi Abd al-Rahman, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Bilamani said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, killed a man from the people of the tribe. He killed a man from the non-Muslims, and he said: I am more deserving of the one who fulfills his obligation. (Daraqutni 135)"
"28032","(28032) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali, and Abdullah; They both said: If he kills a Jew or a Christian, he will be killed."
"28033","(28033) Mu’tamar narrated to us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Maimun bin Mihran; He told him, he said: A Muslim man passed by a Jewish man, and his wife fell in love with him, so he killed him and defeated her. So he wrote to Omar bin Abdul Aziz, and Omar wrote: “Push him to his guardian.” He said: “So We delivered him to his mother,” and she became upset. He covered his head with a rock, or with a prayer, I do not know whether it was clear, or he confessed."
"28034","(28034) Ali bin Misir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Misirah, on the authority of Al-Nazzal bin Sabrah, He said: A man of the knights of the people of Kufa killed a servant of the people of Al-Hira, so Omar wrote: They took his brother away from him, so they pushed back. The man went to my brother Al-Abadi and killed him. Then Omar’s letter came: “Do not kill him” when he had killed him."
"28035","(28035) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A Muslim should be killed in accordance with covenants."
"28036","(28036) Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a Muslim who intentionally kills a non-Muslim, he said: He will be killed for it."
"28037","(28037) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, he said: narrated to us that Omar ibn al-Khattab led A Muslim man with a non-Muslim man."
"28038","(28038) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar Ibn Al-Khattab; He led a man from among the Muslims with a man from the people of Hira."
"28039","(28039) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Musawir, he said: I heard him say: Whoever opposes the protection of Muhammad by killing them, then kill him."
"28040","(28040) Ma’an told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Abdul Rahman; That a man from Nabataean attacked a man from the people of Medina and killed him like a deer, so Aban bin Uthman was brought to him. And when he was in charge of Medina, he ordered the Muslim who killed the non-Muslim to be killed."
"28041","(28041) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Muhammad bin Qays al-Asadi narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Misra, on the authority of al-Nazzal bin I looked at it; That a man from among the Muslims killed a man from the people of Al-Hira, so he wrote about it to Omar ibn Al-Khattab, so Omar wrote: They killed him. With that, it was said to his brother Hunayn: Kill him. He said: Until the wrath comes. He said: Then it reached Omar that he was one of the knights of the Muslims. He said: So Omar wrote: Do not restrict him to it. He said: Then the letter came to him and he had been killed. (Tahawi 196)"
"28042","(28042) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abu Juhayfy, who said: We said to Ali: Do you have anything from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, other than the Qur’an? He said: No, by the one who split the grain and healed the soul, unless God gives you a man who understands the Book of God and what is in this. The newspaper? He said: I said: What is in this document? He said: Reason, and the redemption of a prisoner, and a Muslim is not killed by an infidel. (Bukhari 111, Tirmidhi 1412)"
"28043","(28043) Ibn Abi Zaydah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A believer should not be killed for an unbeliever. (Abu Dawud 2745. Tirmidhi 1413)"
"28044","(28044) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’qil, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A Muslim should not be killed. An unbeliever, and no covenant in his covenant. (Abu Dawud 4519. An-Nasa’i 6936)"
"28045","(28045) Ibn Mushir told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Al-Malih; That a man from his people shot an arrow at a Jewish man and killed him, so it was reported to Omar bin Al-Khattab, and he fined him four thousand, And he did not abstain from it."
"28046","(28046) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He was asked about someone who kills a Jew or a Christian? He said: A Muslim cannot kill an infidel, even if he kills him intentionally."
"28047","(28047) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A Muslim man should not be killed by a Jew, nor As a Christian, but he is charged blood money."
"28048","(28048) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Ali said: It is from the Sunnah that a believer should not be killed. An unbeliever, nor a free slave."
"28049","Abu Abdul Rahman Buqiy bin Mukhlid told us, Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Abi Shaybah Al-Absi told us, he said:\n(28049) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Anas; A Jew smashed a woman’s head with a stone and killed her, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, smashed his head between two stones. (Bukhari 6885. Ahmed 170)"
"28050","(28050) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastawai narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab, that Omar was killed Three people from Sana'a with a woman. (Abdul Razzaq 18073)"
"28051","(28051) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Ibrahim (h) and on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: A man is killed with a woman if he kills her intentionally."
"28052","(28052) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali and Abdullah, who said: If a man kills The woman intentionally, so he is in trouble."
"28053","(28053) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: He will be killed and there is no settlement between them."
"28054","(28054) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: A man who killed a woman was brought before Ali, and he said: Ali to her guardians: If you wish, pay half the blood money and kill him."
"28055","(28055) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The male should not be killed with the female until he has paid half the blood money. His family"
"28056","(28056) Ali told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Regarding a man killing a woman, he said: If they kill him, they pay half the blood money, and if they wish, they accept the blood money."
